."}},"blockId":"exam_01_B_case2"},{"id":"exam_01_B_case2_q2","lessonId":"","position":6,"kind":"numeric","points":0,"required":true,"revision":1,"prompt":{"fr":"Masse 1250 kg ; vitesse 54 km/h ; délai 0,30 s ; décélération demandée 5 m/s² ; cas sec μ = 0,80 ; cas faible adhérence μ = 0,35 ; h = 0,50 m ; L = 2,50 m ; route plane.\n\nCalcule la distance en faible adhérence.","en":"Mass 1250 kg; speed 54 km/h; delay 0.30 s; requested deceleration 5 m/s²; dry μ = 0.80; low-grip μ = 0.35; h = 0.50 m; L = 2.50 m; level road.\n\nCalculate low-grip stopping distance."},"choices":[],"settings":{"unit":"m","toleranceLabel":{"fr":"Tolérance absolue ±0.111796 m.","en":"Absolute tolerance ±0.111796 m."}},"blockId":"exam_01_B_case2"},{"id":"exam_01_B_case2_q3","lessonId":"","position":7,"kind":"numeric","points":0,"required":true,"revision":1,"prompt":{"fr":"Masse 1250 kg ; vitesse 54 km/h ; délai 0,30 s ; décélération demandée 5 m/s² ; cas sec μ = 0,80 ; cas faible adhérence μ = 0,35 ; h = 0,50 m ; L = 2,50 m ; route plane.\n\nCalcule le transfert de charge à 5 m/s².","en":"Mass 1250 kg; speed 54 km/h; delay 0.30 s; requested deceleration 5 m/s²; dry μ = 0.80; low-grip μ = 0.35; h = 0.50 m; L = 2.50 m; level road.\n\nCalculate load transfer at 5 m/s²."},"choices":[],"settings":{"unit":"N","toleranceLabel":{"fr":"Tolérance absolue ±3.75 N.","en":"Absolute tolerance ±3.75 N."}},"blockId":"exam_01_B_case2"},{"id":"exam_01_B_case2_decision","lessonId":"","position":8,"kind":"single_choice","points":0,"required":true,"revision":1,"prompt":{"fr":"Masse 1250 kg ; vitesse 54 km/h ; délai 0,30 s ; décélération demandée 5 m/s² ; cas sec μ = 0,80 ; cas faible adhérence μ = 0,35 ; h = 0,50 m ; L = 2,50 m ; route plane.\n\nRevue technique : quelle décision est défendable avec les données et les limites du cas ?","en":"Mass 1250 kg; speed 54 km/h; delay 0.30 s; requested deceleration 5 m/s²; dry μ = 0.80; low-grip μ = 0.35; h = 0.50 m; L = 2.50 m; level road.\n\nTechnical review: which decision is defensible given the case data and limitations?"},"choices":[{"id":"exam_01_B_case2_decision_c1","position":1,"labels":{"fr":"Borner la décélération par l’adhérence et garder deux scénarios, puis examiner la rampe de freinage.","en":"Bound deceleration by adhesion, retain both scenarios and examine brake build-up."}},{"id":"exam_01_B_case2_decision_c2","position":2,"labels":{"fr":"Conserver 5 m/s² sur faible adhérence parce que le calculateur le demande.","en":"Keep 5 m/s² on low grip because the controller requests it."}},{"id":"exam_01_B_case2_decision_c3","position":3,"labels":{"fr":"Retirer la distance de délai parce que le véhicule est déjà équipé de freins.","en":"Remove delay distance because brakes are installed."}}],"settings":{},"blockId":"exam_01_B_case2"},{"id":"exam_01_B_case3_q1","lessonId":"","position":9,"kind":"numeric","points":0,"required":true,"revision":1,"prompt":{"fr":"Barre pédagogique en traction : F = 11250 N ; A = 95 mm² ; L = 150 mm ; E = 70 000 N/mm² ; densité 2 700 kg/m³. Aucun trou ni flexion dans ce modèle.\n\nCalcule la contrainte nominale.","en":"Educational tension bar: F = 11250 N; A = 95 mm²; L = 150 mm; E = 70,000 N/mm²; density 2,700 kg/m³. No holes or bending in this model.\n\nCalculate nominal stress."},"choices":[],"settings":{"unit":"MPa","toleranceLabel":{"fr":"Tolérance absolue ±0.355263 MPa.","en":"Absolute tolerance ±0.355263 MPa."}},"blockId":"exam_01_B_case3"},{"id":"exam_01_B_case3_q2","lessonId":"","position":10,"kind":"numeric","points":0,"required":true,"revision":1,"prompt":{"fr":"Barre pédagogique en traction : F = 11250 N ; A = 95 mm² ; L = 150 mm ; E = 70 000 N/mm² ; densité 2 700 kg/m³. Aucun trou ni flexion dans ce modèle.\n\nCalcule l’allongement.","en":"Educational tension bar: F = 11250 N; A = 95 mm²; L = 150 mm; E = 70,000 N/mm²; density 2,700 kg/m³. No holes or bending in this model.\n\nCalculate extension."},"choices":[],"settings":{"unit":"mm","toleranceLabel":{"fr":"Tolérance absolue ±0.000761278 mm.","en":"Absolute tolerance ±0.000761278 mm."}},"blockId":"exam_01_B_case3"},{"id":"exam_01_B_case3_q3","lessonId":"","position":11,"kind":"numeric","points":0,"required":true,"revision":1,"prompt":{"fr":"Barre pédagogique en traction : F = 11250 N ; A = 95 mm² ; L = 150 mm ; E = 70 000 N/mm² ; densité 2 700 kg/m³. Aucun trou ni flexion dans ce modèle.\n\nCalcule la contrainte après réduction de section de 20 %.","en":"Educational tension bar: F = 11250 N; A = 95 mm²; L = 150 mm; E = 70,000 N/mm²; density 2,700 kg/m³. No holes or bending in this model.\n\nCalculate stress after a 20% area reduction."},"choices":[],"settings":{"unit":"MPa","toleranceLabel":{"fr":"Tolérance absolue ±0.444079 MPa.","en":"Absolute tolerance ±0.444079 MPa."}},"blockId":"exam_01_B_case3"},{"id":"exam_01_B_case3_decision","lessonId":"","position":12,"kind":"single_choice","points":0,"required":true,"revision":1,"prompt":{"fr":"Barre pédagogique en traction : F = 11250 N ; A = 95 mm² ; L = 150 mm ; E = 70 000 N/mm² ; densité 2 700 kg/m³. Aucun trou ni flexion dans ce modèle.\n\nRevue technique : quelle décision est défendable avec les données et les limites du cas ?","en":"Educational tension bar: F = 11250 N; A = 95 mm²; L = 150 mm; E = 70,000 N/mm²; density 2,700 kg/m³. No holes or bending in this model.\n\nTechnical review: which decision is defensible given the case data and limitations?"},"choices":[{"id":"exam_01_B_case3_decision_c1","position":1,"labels":{"fr":"Valider le crash à partir de la seule contrainte nominale.","en":"Approve crash performance from nominal stress alone."}},{"id":"exam_01_B_case3_decision_c2","position":2,"labels":{"fr":"Affirmer que réduire la section réduit aussi la contrainte parce que la pièce est plus légère.","en":"Claim reducing area also reduces stress because the part is lighter."}},{"id":"exam_01_B_case3_decision_c3","position":3,"labels":{"fr":"Vérifier la limite, les concentrations, la fatigue et les fixations avant d’appliquer cette réduction à un support.","en":"Check limits, concentrations, fatigue and joints before applying this reduction to a bracket."}}],"settings":{},"blockId":"exam_01_B_case3"}]'::jsonb,'{"exam_01_B_case1_q1":{"answer":{"value":148.8372093023256,"unit":"km","abs_tolerance":0.4465116279069768},"rubric":{},"explanation":{"fr":"1. Énergie utile : 32 × 0,80 = 25.6 kWh.\n2. Convertir en Wh : 25600 Wh.\n3. Autonomie nominale : 25600 / 172 = 148.8372 km.\n4. Autonomie dégradée : 25600 / 192 = 133.3333 km.\n5. Besoin utile pour 150 km dégradés : 150 × 192/1000 = 28.8 kWh. Comparer séparément chaque scénario à 150 km.\n\nLa consommation est supposée constante et indépendante de la masse ; le résultat ne prouve pas une autonomie sur cycle réel.","en":"1. Usable energy: 32 × 0.80 = 25.6 kWh.\n2. Convert to Wh: 25600 Wh.\n3. Nominal range: 25600 / 172 = 148.8372 km.\n4. Degraded range: 25600 / 192 = 133.3333 km.\n5. Usable energy for 150 degraded kilometres: 150 × 192/1000 = 28.8 kWh. Compare each scenario separately with 150 km.\n\nConsumption is assumed constant and independent of mass; this does not establish actual drive-cycle range."}},"exam_01_B_case1_q2":{"answer":{"value":133.33333333333334,"unit":"km","abs_tolerance":0.4},"rubric":{},"explanation":{"fr":"1. Énergie utile : 32 × 0,80 = 25.6 kWh.\n2. Convertir en Wh : 25600 Wh.\n3. Autonomie nominale : 25600 / 172 = 148.8372 km.\n4. Autonomie dégradée : 25600 / 192 = 133.3333 km.\n5. Besoin utile pour 150 km dégradés : 150 × 192/1000 = 28.8 kWh. Comparer séparément chaque scénario à 150 km.\n\nLa consommation est supposée constante et indépendante de la masse ; le résultat ne prouve pas une autonomie sur cycle réel.","en":"1. Usable energy: 32 × 0.80 = 25.6 kWh.\n2. Convert to Wh: 25600 Wh.\n3. Nominal range: 25600 / 172 = 148.8372 km.\n4. Degraded range: 25600 / 192 = 133.3333 km.\n5. Usable energy for 150 degraded kilometres: 150 × 192/1000 = 28.8 kWh. Compare each scenario separately with 150 km.\n\nConsumption is assumed constant and independent of mass; this does not establish actual drive-cycle range."}},"exam_01_B_case1_q3":{"answer":{"value":28.8,"unit":"kWh","abs_tolerance":0.0864},"rubric":{},"explanation":{"fr":"1. Énergie utile : 32 × 0,80 = 25.6 kWh.\n2. Convertir en Wh : 25600 Wh.\n3. Autonomie nominale : 25600 / 172 = 148.8372 km.\n4. Autonomie dégradée : 25600 / 192 = 133.3333 km.\n5. Besoin utile pour 150 km dégradés : 150 × 192/1000 = 28.8 kWh. Comparer séparément chaque scénario à 150 km.\n\nLa consommation est supposée constante et indépendante de la masse ; le résultat ne prouve pas une autonomie sur cycle réel.","en":"1. Usable energy: 32 × 0.80 = 25.6 kWh.\n2. Convert to Wh: 25600 Wh.\n3. Nominal range: 25600 / 172 = 148.8372 km.\n4. Degraded range: 25600 / 192 = 133.3333 km.\n5. Usable energy for 150 degraded kilometres: 150 × 192/1000 = 28.8 kWh. Compare each scenario separately with 150 km.\n\nConsumption is assumed constant and independent of mass; this does not establish actual drive-cycle range."}},"exam_01_B_case1_decision":{"answer":{"choice_id":"exam_01_B_case1_decision_c2"},"rubric":{},"explanation":{"fr":"Conserver deux verdicts conditionnels et étudier masse, thermique et consommation avant d’augmenter la batterie. La consommation est supposée constante et indépendante de la masse ; le résultat ne prouve pas une autonomie sur cycle réel.","en":"Keep separate conditional verdicts and examine mass, thermal limits and consumption before increasing battery capacity. Consumption is assumed constant and independent of mass; this does not establish actual drive-cycle range."}},"exam_01_B_case2_q1":{"answer":{"value":27.0,"unit":"m","abs_tolerance":0.081},"rubric":{},"explanation":{"fr":"1. v = 15 m/s.\n2. À sec μg = 7,848 m/s² : a = 5 ; d = 27 m.\n3. Faible adhérence μg = 3,4335 m/s² : d = 37.2654 m.\n4. Transfert à a = 5 : 1250 N de l’arrière vers l’avant.\n5. Le verdict de chaque cible reste lié à son coefficient μ et à sa vitesse.\n\nDécélération constante après délai, sans pente ni variation de μ.","en":"1. v = 15 m/s.\n2. Dry μg = 7.848 m/s²: a = 5; d = 27 m.\n3. Low-grip μg = 3.4335 m/s²: d = 37.2654 m.\n4. Load transfer at a = 5: 1250 N rear to front.\n5. Each target verdict retains its own μ and speed conditions.\n\nConstant deceleration after delay, no grade or varying μ."}},"exam_01_B_case2_q2":{"answer":{"value":37.265399737876805,"unit":"m","abs_tolerance":0.11179619921363042},"rubric":{},"explanation":{"fr":"1. v = 15 m/s.\n2. À sec μg = 7,848 m/s² : a = 5 ; d = 27 m.\n3. Faible adhérence μg = 3,4335 m/s² : d = 37.2654 m.\n4. Transfert à a = 5 : 1250 N de l’arrière vers l’avant.\n5. Le verdict de chaque cible reste lié à son coefficient μ et à sa vitesse.\n\nDécélération constante après délai, sans pente ni variation de μ.","en":"1. v = 15 m/s.\n2. Dry μg = 7.848 m/s²: a = 5; d = 27 m.\n3. Low-grip μg = 3.4335 m/s²: d = 37.2654 m.\n4. Load transfer at a = 5: 1250 N rear to front.\n5. Each target verdict retains its own μ and speed conditions.\n\nConstant deceleration after delay, no grade or varying μ."}},"exam_01_B_case2_q3":{"answer":{"value":1250.0,"unit":"N","abs_tolerance":3.75},"rubric":{},"explanation":{"fr":"1. v = 15 m/s.\n2. À sec μg = 7,848 m/s² : a = 5 ; d = 27 m.\n3. Faible adhérence μg = 3,4335 m/s² : d = 37.2654 m.\n4. Transfert à a = 5 : 1250 N de l’arrière vers l’avant.\n5. Le verdict de chaque cible reste lié à son coefficient μ et à sa vitesse.\n\nDécélération constante après délai, sans pente ni variation de μ.","en":"1. v = 15 m/s.\n2. Dry μg = 7.848 m/s²: a = 5; d = 27 m.\n3. Low-grip μg = 3.4335 m/s²: d = 37.2654 m.\n4. Load transfer at a = 5: 1250 N rear to front.\n5. Each target verdict retains its own μ and speed conditions.\n\nConstant deceleration after delay, no grade or varying μ."}},"exam_01_B_case2_decision":{"answer":{"choice_id":"exam_01_B_case2_decision_c1"},"rubric":{},"explanation":{"fr":"Borner la décélération par l’adhérence et garder deux scénarios, puis examiner la rampe de freinage. Décélération constante après délai, sans pente ni variation de μ.","en":"Bound deceleration by adhesion, retain both scenarios and examine brake build-up. Constant deceleration after delay, no grade or varying μ."}},"exam_01_B_case3_q1":{"answer":{"value":118.42105263157895,"unit":"MPa","abs_tolerance":0.35526315789473684},"rubric":{},"explanation":{"fr":"1. Contrainte = 11250/95 = 118.4211 N/mm² = MPa.\n2. Allongement = 11250 × 150/(70000 × 95) = 0.2538 mm.\n3. Volume = 95 × 150 mm³ = 0 m³ ; masse = 0.0385 kg.\n4. Une réduction de 20 % de A multiplie contrainte et allongement par 1/0,8 = 1,25.\n\nTraction uniforme seulement : aucun dimensionnement de structure véhicule réelle.","en":"1. Stress = 11250/95 = 118.4211 N/mm² = MPa.\n2. Extension = 11250 × 150/(70000 × 95) = 0.2538 mm.\n3. Volume = 95 × 150 mm³ = 0 m³; mass = 0.0385 kg.\n4. Reducing A by 20% multiplies stress and extension by 1/0.8 = 1.25.\n\nUniform tension only: not real vehicle structural sizing."}},"exam_01_B_case3_q2":{"answer":{"value":0.25375939849624063,"unit":"mm","abs_tolerance":0.0007612781954887219},"rubric":{},"explanation":{"fr":"1. Contrainte = 11250/95 = 118.4211 N/mm² = MPa.\n2. Allongement = 11250 × 150/(70000 × 95) = 0.2538 mm.\n3. Volume = 95 × 150 mm³ = 0 m³ ; masse = 0.0385 kg.\n4. Une réduction de 20 % de A multiplie contrainte et allongement par 1/0,8 = 1,25.\n\nTraction uniforme seulement : aucun dimensionnement de structure véhicule réelle.","en":"1. Stress = 11250/95 = 118.4211 N/mm² = MPa.\n2. Extension = 11250 × 150/(70000 × 95) = 0.2538 mm.\n3. Volume = 95 × 150 mm³ = 0 m³; mass = 0.0385 kg.\n4. Reducing A by 20% multiplies stress and extension by 1/0.8 = 1.25.\n\nUniform tension only: not real vehicle structural sizing."}},"exam_01_B_case3_q3":{"answer":{"value":148.02631578947367,"unit":"MPa","abs_tolerance":0.444078947368421},"rubric":{},"explanation":{"fr":"1. Contrainte = 11250/95 = 118.4211 N/mm² = MPa.\n2. Allongement = 11250 × 150/(70000 × 95) = 0.2538 mm.\n3. Volume = 95 × 150 mm³ = 0 m³ ; masse = 0.0385 kg.\n4. Une réduction de 20 % de A multiplie contrainte et allongement par 1/0,8 = 1,25.\n\nTraction uniforme seulement : aucun dimensionnement de structure véhicule réelle.","en":"1. Stress = 11250/95 = 118.4211 N/mm² = MPa.\n2. Extension = 11250 × 150/(70000 × 95) = 0.2538 mm.\n3. Volume = 95 × 150 mm³ = 0 m³; mass = 0.0385 kg.\n4. Reducing A by 20% multiplies stress and extension by 1/0.8 = 1.25.\n\nUniform tension only: not real vehicle structural sizing."}},"exam_01_B_case3_decision":{"answer":{"choice_id":"exam_01_B_case3_decision_c3"},"rubric":{},"explanation":{"fr":"Vérifier la limite, les concentrations, la fatigue et les fixations avant d’appliquer cette réduction à un support. Traction uniforme seulement : aucun dimensionnement de structure véhicule réelle.","en":"Check limits, concentrations, fatigue and joints before applying this reduction to a bracket. Uniform tension only: not real vehicle structural sizing."}}}'::jsonb) ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
