e technique : quelle décision est défendable avec les données et les limites du cas ?","en":"40 applicable requirements; 37 have approved evidence; 29 tests executed, 27 passed and 2 failed. One failure is critical. The populations are distinct.\n\nTechnical review: which decision is defensible given the case data and limitations?"},"choices":[{"id":"exam_02_B_case2_decision_c1","position":1,"labels":{"fr":"Moyenner les deux pourcentages pour annoncer une conformité véhicule unique.","en":"Average the percentages to announce a single vehicle-compliance rate."}},{"id":"exam_02_B_case2_decision_c2","position":2,"labels":{"fr":"Reclasser les deux échecs comme non exécutés pour améliorer le taux.","en":"Reclassify failures as not executed to improve the rate."}},{"id":"exam_02_B_case2_decision_c3","position":3,"labels":{"fr":"Garder visibles l’échec critique, les exigences sans preuve et les configurations ; décider un plan de fermeture.","en":"Keep the critical failure, unproven requirements and configurations visible; decide a closure plan."}}],"settings":{},"blockId":"exam_02_B_case2"},{"id":"exam_02_B_case3_q1","lessonId":"","position":9,"kind":"numeric","points":0,"required":true,"revision":1,"prompt":{"fr":"Batterie brute 27 kWh ; fenêtre utile 80 % ; consommation nominale 137 Wh/km, scénario dégradé 157 Wh/km ; cible 150 km.\n\nCalcule l’autonomie nominale.","en":"Gross battery 27 kWh; usable window 80%; nominal consumption 137 Wh/km, degraded case 157 Wh/km; target 150 km.\n\nCalculate nominal range."},"choices":[],"settings":{"unit":"km","toleranceLabel":{"fr":"Tolérance absolue ±0.472993 km.","en":"Absolute tolerance ±0.472993 km."}},"blockId":"exam_02_B_case3"},{"id":"exam_02_B_case3_q2","lessonId":"","position":10,"kind":"numeric","points":0,"required":true,"revision":1,"prompt":{"fr":"Batterie brute 27 kWh ; fenêtre utile 80 % ; consommation nominale 137 Wh/km, scénario dégradé 157 Wh/km ; cible 150 km.\n\nCalcule l’autonomie dans le scénario dégradé.","en":"Gross battery 27 kWh; usable window 80%; nominal consumption 137 Wh/km, degraded case 157 Wh/km; target 150 km.\n\nCalculate degraded-case range."},"choices":[],"settings":{"unit":"km","toleranceLabel":{"fr":"Tolérance absolue ±0.412739 km.","en":"Absolute tolerance ±0.412739 km."}},"blockId":"exam_02_B_case3"},{"id":"exam_02_B_case3_q3","lessonId":"","position":11,"kind":"numeric","points":0,"required":true,"revision":1,"prompt":{"fr":"Batterie brute 27 kWh ; fenêtre utile 80 % ; consommation nominale 137 Wh/km, scénario dégradé 157 Wh/km ; cible 150 km.\n\nCalcule l’énergie utile nécessaire pour 150 km dégradés.","en":"Gross battery 27 kWh; usable window 80%; nominal consumption 137 Wh/km, degraded case 157 Wh/km; target 150 km.\n\nCalculate usable energy needed for 150 degraded kilometres."},"choices":[],"settings":{"unit":"kWh","toleranceLabel":{"fr":"Tolérance absolue ±0.07065 kWh.","en":"Absolute tolerance ±0.07065 kWh."}},"blockId":"exam_02_B_case3"},{"id":"exam_02_B_case3_decision","lessonId":"","position":12,"kind":"single_choice","points":0,"required":true,"revision":1,"prompt":{"fr":"Batterie brute 27 kWh ; fenêtre utile 80 % ; consommation nominale 137 Wh/km, scénario dégradé 157 Wh/km ; cible 150 km.\n\nRevue technique : quelle décision est défendable avec les données et les limites du cas ?","en":"Gross battery 27 kWh; usable window 80%; nominal consumption 137 Wh/km, degraded case 157 Wh/km; target 150 km.\n\nTechnical review: which decision is defensible given the case data and limitations?"},"choices":[{"id":"exam_02_B_case3_decision_c1","position":1,"labels":{"fr":"Moyenner les deux autonomies pour déclarer la cible satisfaite dans les deux cas.","en":"Average both ranges to declare that both scenarios meet the target."}},{"id":"exam_02_B_case3_decision_c2","position":2,"labels":{"fr":"Conserver deux verdicts conditionnels et étudier masse, thermique et consommation avant d’augmenter la batterie.","en":"Keep separate conditional verdicts and examine mass, thermal limits and consumption before increasing battery capacity."}},{"id":"exam_02_B_case3_decision_c3","position":3,"labels":{"fr":"Utiliser l’énergie brute pour tous les scénarios, puisque la fenêtre ne change que la recharge.","en":"Use gross energy in every scenario because the window only affects charging."}}],"settings":{},"blockId":"exam_02_B_case3"}]'::jsonb,'{"exam_02_B_case1_q1":{"answer":{"value":140,"unit":"code","abs_tolerance":0.01},"rubric":{},"explanation":{"fr":"1. Valeur entière = 14/0,1 = 140.\n2. Octets décimaux little-endian : [140, 0] ; hex : [8C, 00].\n3. Lecture inversée : 256×140+0 = 35840 pas ; couple apparent 3584 N·m.\n4. Un aller-retour indépendant vérifie le codage ; domaine, validité et timeout demandent d’autres tests.\n\nLe contrat de cet exercice est uint16. Domaine, saturation et validité demandent des tests supplémentaires.","en":"1. Integer = 14/0.1 = 140.\n2. Little-endian decimal bytes: [140, 0]; hex: [8C, 00].\n3. Reversed decoding: 256×140+0 = 35840 counts; apparent torque 3584 N·m.\n4. An independent round trip checks encoding; range, validity and timeout require additional tests.\n\nThis exercise uses uint16. Range, saturation and validity need additional tests."}},"exam_02_B_case1_q2":{"answer":{"value":3584.0,"unit":"N·m","abs_tolerance":10.752},"rubric":{},"explanation":{"fr":"1. Valeur entière = 14/0,1 = 140.\n2. Octets décimaux little-endian : [140, 0] ; hex : [8C, 00].\n3. Lecture inversée : 256×140+0 = 35840 pas ; couple apparent 3584 N·m.\n4. Un aller-retour indépendant vérifie le codage ; domaine, validité et timeout demandent d’autres tests.\n\nLe contrat de cet exercice est uint16. Domaine, saturation et validité demandent des tests supplémentaires.","en":"1. Integer = 14/0.1 = 140.\n2. Little-endian decimal bytes: [140, 0]; hex: [8C, 00].\n3. Reversed decoding: 256×140+0 = 35840 counts; apparent torque 3584 N·m.\n4. An independent round trip checks encoding; range, validity and timeout require additional tests.\n\nThis exercise uses uint16. Range, saturation and validity need additional tests."}},"exam_02_B_case1_q3":{"answer":{"value":140,"unit":"octet","abs_tolerance":0.01},"rubric":{},"explanation":{"fr":"1. Valeur entière = 14/0,1 = 140.\n2. Octets décimaux little-endian : [140, 0] ; hex : [8C, 00].\n3. Lecture inversée : 256×140+0 = 35840 pas ; couple apparent 3584 N·m.\n4. Un aller-retour indépendant vérifie le codage ; domaine, validité et timeout demandent d’autres tests.\n\nLe contrat de cet exercice est uint16. Domaine, saturation et validité demandent des tests supplémentaires.","en":"1. Integer = 14/0.1 = 140.\n2. Little-endian decimal bytes: [140, 0]; hex: [8C, 00].\n3. Reversed decoding: 256×140+0 = 35840 counts; apparent torque 3584 N·m.\n4. An independent round trip checks encoding; range, validity and timeout require additional tests.\n\nThis exercise uses uint16. Range, saturation and validity need additional tests."}},"exam_02_B_case1_decision":{"answer":{"choice_id":"exam_02_B_case1_decision_c1"},"rubric":{},"explanation":{"fr":"Fixer et tester unité, signe, ordre des octets, domaine et réaction au défaut dans l’ICD. Le contrat de cet exercice est uint16. Domaine, saturation et validité demandent des tests supplémentaires.","en":"Specify and test unit, sign, byte order, range and fault response in the ICD. This exercise uses uint16. Range, saturation and validity need additional tests."}},"exam_02_B_case2_q1":{"answer":{"value":92.5,"unit":"%","abs_tolerance":0.2775},"rubric":{},"explanation":{"fr":"1. Couverture exigences = 37/40×100 = 92.5 %.\n2. Réussite essais = 27/29×100 = 93.1034 %.\n3. Exigences sans preuve approuvée = 3.\n4. Le dénominateur des essais ne remplace pas celui des exigences. L’échec critique doit être traité explicitement, quel que soit le pourcentage.\n\nLes comptes sont fictifs et n’établissent pas la qualité des méthodes de preuve.","en":"1. Requirement coverage = 37/40×100 = 92.5%.\n2. Test pass rate = 27/29×100 = 93.1034%.\n3. Requirements without approved evidence = 3.\n4. Test and requirement denominators are not interchangeable. Address the critical failure explicitly regardless of percentage.\n\nCounts are fictional and do not establish evidence-method quality."}},"exam_02_B_case2_q2":{"answer":{"value":93.10344827586206,"unit":"%","abs_tolerance":0.2793103448275862},"rubric":{},"explanation":{"fr":"1. Couverture exigences = 37/40×100 = 92.5 %.\n2. Réussite essais = 27/29×100 = 93.1034 %.\n3. Exigences sans preuve approuvée = 3.\n4. Le dénominateur des essais ne remplace pas celui des exigences. L’échec critique doit être traité explicitement, quel que soit le pourcentage.\n\nLes comptes sont fictifs et n’établissent pas la qualité des méthodes de preuve.","en":"1. Requirement coverage = 37/40×100 = 92.5%.\n2. Test pass rate = 27/29×100 = 93.1034%.\n3. Requirements without approved evidence = 3.\n4. Test and requirement denominators are not interchangeable. Address the critical failure explicitly regardless of percentage.\n\nCounts are fictional and do not establish evidence-method quality."}},"exam_02_B_case2_q3":{"answer":{"value":3,"unit":"exigences","abs_tolerance":0.01},"rubric":{},"explanation":{"fr":"1. Couverture exigences = 37/40×100 = 92.5 %.\n2. Réussite essais = 27/29×100 = 93.1034 %.\n3. Exigences sans preuve approuvée = 3.\n4. Le dénominateur des essais ne remplace pas celui des exigences. L’échec critique doit être traité explicitement, quel que soit le pourcentage.\n\nLes comptes sont fictifs et n’établissent pas la qualité des méthodes de preuve.","en":"1. Requirement coverage = 37/40×100 = 92.5%.\n2. Test pass rate = 27/29×100 = 93.1034%.\n3. Requirements without approved evidence = 3.\n4. Test and requirement denominators are not interchangeable. Address the critical failure explicitly regardless of percentage.\n\nCounts are fictional and do not establish evidence-method quality."}},"exam_02_B_case2_decision":{"answer":{"choice_id":"exam_02_B_case2_decision_c3"},"rubric":{},"explanation":{"fr":"Garder visibles l’échec critique, les exigences sans preuve et les configurations ; décider un plan de fermeture. Les comptes sont fictifs et n’établissent pas la qualité des méthodes de preuve.","en":"Keep the critical failure, unproven requirements and configurations visible; decide a closure plan. Counts are fictional and do not establish evidence-method quality."}},"exam_02_B_case3_q1":{"answer":{"value":157.66423357664235,"unit":"km","abs_tolerance":0.47299270072992705},"rubric":{},"explanation":{"fr":"1. Énergie utile : 27 × 0,80 = 21.6 kWh.\n2. Convertir en Wh : 21600 Wh.\n3. Autonomie nominale : 21600 / 137 = 157.6642 km.\n4. Autonomie dégradée : 21600 / 157 = 137.5796 km.\n5. Besoin utile pour 150 km dégradés : 150 × 157/1000 = 23.55 kWh. Comparer séparément chaque scénario à 150 km.\n\nLa consommation est supposée constante et indépendante de la masse ; le résultat ne prouve pas une autonomie sur cycle réel.","en":"1. Usable energy: 27 × 0.80 = 21.6 kWh.\n2. Convert to Wh: 21600 Wh.\n3. Nominal range: 21600 / 137 = 157.6642 km.\n4. Degraded range: 21600 / 157 = 137.5796 km.\n5. Usable energy for 150 degraded kilometres: 150 × 157/1000 = 23.55 kWh. Compare each scenario separately with 150 km.\n\nConsumption is assumed constant and independent of mass; this does not establish actual drive-cycle range."}},"exam_02_B_case3_q2":{"answer":{"value":137.5796178343949,"unit":"km","abs_tolerance":0.4127388535031847},"rubric":{},"explanation":{"fr":"1. Énergie utile : 27 × 0,80 = 21.6 kWh.\n2. Convertir en Wh : 21600 Wh.\n3. Autonomie nominale : 21600 / 137 = 157.6642 km.\n4. Autonomie dégradée : 21600 / 157 = 137.5796 km.\n5. Besoin utile pour 150 km dégradés : 150 × 157/1000 = 23.55 kWh. Comparer séparément chaque scénario à 150 km.\n\nLa consommation est supposée constante et indépendante de la masse ; le résultat ne prouve pas une autonomie sur cycle réel.","en":"1. Usable energy: 27 × 0.80 = 21.6 kWh.\n2. Convert to Wh: 21600 Wh.\n3. Nominal range: 21600 / 137 = 157.6642 km.\n4. Degraded range: 21600 / 157 = 137.5796 km.\n5. Usable energy for 150 degraded kilometres: 150 × 157/1000 = 23.55 kWh. Compare each scenario separately with 150 km.\n\nConsumption is assumed constant and independent of mass; this does not establish actual drive-cycle range."}},"exam_02_B_case3_q3":{"answer":{"value":23.55,"unit":"kWh","abs_tolerance":0.07065},"rubric":{},"explanation":{"fr":"1. Énergie utile : 27 × 0,80 = 21.6 kWh.\n2. Convertir en Wh : 21600 Wh.\n3. Autonomie nominale : 21600 / 137 = 157.6642 km.\n4. Autonomie dégradée : 21600 / 157 = 137.5796 km.\n5. Besoin utile pour 150 km dégradés : 150 × 157/1000 = 23.55 kWh. Comparer séparément chaque scénario à 150 km.\n\nLa consommation est supposée constante et indépendante de la masse ; le résultat ne prouve pas une autonomie sur cycle réel.","en":"1. Usable energy: 27 × 0.80 = 21.6 kWh.\n2. Convert to Wh: 21600 Wh.\n3. Nominal range: 21600 / 137 = 157.6642 km.\n4. Degraded range: 21600 / 157 = 137.5796 km.\n5. Usable energy for 150 degraded kilometres: 150 × 157/1000 = 23.55 kWh. Compare each scenario separately with 150 km.\n\nConsumption is assumed constant and independent of mass; this does not establish actual drive-cycle range."}},"exam_02_B_case3_decision":{"answer":{"choice_id":"exam_02_B_case3_decision_c2"},"rubric":{},"explanation":{"fr":"Conserver deux verdicts conditionnels et étudier masse, thermique et consommation avant d’augmenter la batterie. La consommation est supposée constante et indépendante de la masse ; le résultat ne prouve pas une autonomie sur cycle réel.","en":"Keep separate conditional verdicts and examine mass, thermal limits and consumption before increasing battery capacity. Consumption is assumed constant and independent of mass; this does not establish actual drive-cycle range."}}}'::jsonb) ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
