idence; 28 tests executed, 26 passed and 2 failed. One failure is critical. The populations are distinct.\n\nCalculate executed-test pass rate."},"choices":[],"settings":{"unit":"%","toleranceLabel":{"fr":"Tolérance absolue ±0.278571 %.","en":"Absolute tolerance ±0.278571 %."}},"blockId":"exam_03_B_case3"},{"id":"exam_03_B_case3_q3","lessonId":"","position":11,"kind":"numeric","points":0,"required":true,"revision":1,"prompt":{"fr":"38 exigences applicables ; 35 ont une preuve approuvée ; 28 essais exécutés, dont 26 réussis et 2 échoués. Un échec est critique. Les deux populations sont distinctes.\n\nCompte les exigences sans preuve approuvée.","en":"38 applicable requirements; 35 have approved evidence; 28 tests executed, 26 passed and 2 failed. One failure is critical. The populations are distinct.\n\nCount requirements without approved evidence."},"choices":[],"settings":{"unit":"exigences","toleranceLabel":{"fr":"Tolérance absolue ±0.01 exigences.","en":"Absolute tolerance ±0.01 exigences."}},"blockId":"exam_03_B_case3"},{"id":"exam_03_B_case3_decision","lessonId":"","position":12,"kind":"single_choice","points":0,"required":true,"revision":1,"prompt":{"fr":"38 exigences applicables ; 35 ont une preuve approuvée ; 28 essais exécutés, dont 26 réussis et 2 échoués. Un échec est critique. Les deux populations sont distinctes.\n\nRevue technique : quelle décision est défendable avec les données et les limites du cas ?","en":"38 applicable requirements; 35 have approved evidence; 28 tests executed, 26 passed and 2 failed. One failure is critical. The populations are distinct.\n\nTechnical review: which decision is defensible given the case data and limitations?"},"choices":[{"id":"exam_03_B_case3_decision_c1","position":1,"labels":{"fr":"Garder visibles l’échec critique, les exigences sans preuve et les configurations ; décider un plan de fermeture.","en":"Keep the critical failure, unproven requirements and configurations visible; decide a closure plan."}},{"id":"exam_03_B_case3_decision_c2","position":2,"labels":{"fr":"Moyenner les deux pourcentages pour annoncer une conformité véhicule unique.","en":"Average the percentages to announce a single vehicle-compliance rate."}},{"id":"exam_03_B_case3_decision_c3","position":3,"labels":{"fr":"Reclasser les deux échecs comme non exécutés pour améliorer le taux.","en":"Reclassify failures as not executed to improve the rate."}}],"settings":{},"blockId":"exam_03_B_case3"}]'::jsonb,'{"exam_03_B_case1_q1":{"answer":{"value":50100,"unit":"€","abs_tolerance":150.3},"rubric":{},"explanation":{"fr":"1. Récurrent = 1300×17 = 22100 €.\n2. Fixe = 18000+7000+3000 = 28000 €.\n3. Impact total = 50100 €.\n4. Impact moyen sur population = 38.5385 €/véhicule ; ce n’est pas le nouveau coût récurrent.\n5. Impact exigences, interfaces et preuves reste à analyser.\n\nPas de coût délai ni de retour terrain inclus ; annoncer clairement ces exclusions.","en":"1. Recurring = 1300×17 = €22100.\n2. Fixed = 18000+7000+3000 = €28000.\n3. Total impact = €50100.\n4. Average population impact = €38.5385/vehicle, not the new recurring cost.\n5. Requirement, interface and evidence impacts still need analysis.\n\nSchedule and field-return costs are excluded and must be declared."}},"exam_03_B_case1_q2":{"answer":{"value":38.53846153846154,"unit":"€/véhicule","abs_tolerance":0.11561538461538462},"rubric":{},"explanation":{"fr":"1. Récurrent = 1300×17 = 22100 €.\n2. Fixe = 18000+7000+3000 = 28000 €.\n3. Impact total = 50100 €.\n4. Impact moyen sur population = 38.5385 €/véhicule ; ce n’est pas le nouveau coût récurrent.\n5. Impact exigences, interfaces et preuves reste à analyser.\n\nPas de coût délai ni de retour terrain inclus ; annoncer clairement ces exclusions.","en":"1. Recurring = 1300×17 = €22100.\n2. Fixed = 18000+7000+3000 = €28000.\n3. Total impact = €50100.\n4. Average population impact = €38.5385/vehicle, not the new recurring cost.\n5. Requirement, interface and evidence impacts still need analysis.\n\nSchedule and field-return costs are excluded and must be declared."}},"exam_03_B_case1_q3":{"answer":{"value":22100,"unit":"€","abs_tolerance":66.3},"rubric":{},"explanation":{"fr":"1. Récurrent = 1300×17 = 22100 €.\n2. Fixe = 18000+7000+3000 = 28000 €.\n3. Impact total = 50100 €.\n4. Impact moyen sur population = 38.5385 €/véhicule ; ce n’est pas le nouveau coût récurrent.\n5. Impact exigences, interfaces et preuves reste à analyser.\n\nPas de coût délai ni de retour terrain inclus ; annoncer clairement ces exclusions.","en":"1. Recurring = 1300×17 = €22100.\n2. Fixed = 18000+7000+3000 = €28000.\n3. Total impact = €50100.\n4. Average population impact = €38.5385/vehicle, not the new recurring cost.\n5. Requirement, interface and evidence impacts still need analysis.\n\nSchedule and field-return costs are excluded and must be declared."}},"exam_03_B_case1_decision":{"answer":{"choice_id":"exam_03_B_case1_decision_c3"},"rubric":{},"explanation":{"fr":"Décider après analyse technique, puis fixer effectivité, non-régression et fermeture documentée. Pas de coût délai ni de retour terrain inclus ; annoncer clairement ces exclusions.","en":"Decide after technical analysis, then set effectivity, regression evidence and documented closure. Schedule and field-return costs are excluded and must be declared."}},"exam_03_B_case2_q1":{"answer":{"value":92.72727272727272,"unit":"%","abs_tolerance":0.27818181818181814},"rubric":{},"explanation":{"fr":"1. FPY = 1020/1100×100 = 92.7273 %.\n2. Rendement final = (1020+50)/1100×100 = 97.2727 %.\n3. Rebuts = 1100−1020−50 = 30.\n4. Les 50 reprises coûtent du temps et des ressources, même si elles sont finalement bonnes.\n\nLe rendement seul ne démontre ni capabilité ni stabilité du procédé.","en":"1. FPY = 1020/1100×100 = 92.7273%.\n2. Final yield = (1020+50)/1100×100 = 97.2727%.\n3. Scrap = 1100−1020−50 = 30.\n4. Rework consumes time and resources even when the units ultimately pass.\n\nYield alone establishes neither capability nor process stability."}},"exam_03_B_case2_q2":{"answer":{"value":97.27272727272728,"unit":"%","abs_tolerance":0.29181818181818187},"rubric":{},"explanation":{"fr":"1. FPY = 1020/1100×100 = 92.7273 %.\n2. Rendement final = (1020+50)/1100×100 = 97.2727 %.\n3. Rebuts = 1100−1020−50 = 30.\n4. Les 50 reprises coûtent du temps et des ressources, même si elles sont finalement bonnes.\n\nLe rendement seul ne démontre ni capabilité ni stabilité du procédé.","en":"1. FPY = 1020/1100×100 = 92.7273%.\n2. Final yield = (1020+50)/1100×100 = 97.2727%.\n3. Scrap = 1100−1020−50 = 30.\n4. Rework consumes time and resources even when the units ultimately pass.\n\nYield alone establishes neither capability nor process stability."}},"exam_03_B_case2_q3":{"answer":{"value":30,"unit":"unités","abs_tolerance":0.01},"rubric":{},"explanation":{"fr":"1. FPY = 1020/1100×100 = 92.7273 %.\n2. Rendement final = (1020+50)/1100×100 = 97.2727 %.\n3. Rebuts = 1100−1020−50 = 30.\n4. Les 50 reprises coûtent du temps et des ressources, même si elles sont finalement bonnes.\n\nLe rendement seul ne démontre ni capabilité ni stabilité du procédé.","en":"1. FPY = 1020/1100×100 = 92.7273%.\n2. Final yield = (1020+50)/1100×100 = 97.2727%.\n3. Scrap = 1100−1020−50 = 30.\n4. Rework consumes time and resources even when the units ultimately pass.\n\nYield alone establishes neither capability nor process stability."}},"exam_03_B_case2_decision":{"answer":{"choice_id":"exam_03_B_case2_decision_c2"},"rubric":{},"explanation":{"fr":"Suivre premier passage, retouches et rebuts séparément, puis démontrer une cause avant correction. Le rendement seul ne démontre ni capabilité ni stabilité du procédé.","en":"Track first pass, rework and scrap separately, then demonstrate a cause before correcting. Yield alone establishes neither capability nor process stability."}},"exam_03_B_case3_q1":{"answer":{"value":92.10526315789474,"unit":"%","abs_tolerance":0.27631578947368424},"rubric":{},"explanation":{"fr":"1. Couverture exigences = 35/38×100 = 92.1053 %.\n2. Réussite essais = 26/28×100 = 92.8571 %.\n3. Exigences sans preuve approuvée = 3.\n4. Le dénominateur des essais ne remplace pas celui des exigences. L’échec critique doit être traité explicitement, quel que soit le pourcentage.\n\nLes comptes sont fictifs et n’établissent pas la qualité des méthodes de preuve.","en":"1. Requirement coverage = 35/38×100 = 92.1053%.\n2. Test pass rate = 26/28×100 = 92.8571%.\n3. Requirements without approved evidence = 3.\n4. Test and requirement denominators are not interchangeable. Address the critical failure explicitly regardless of percentage.\n\nCounts are fictional and do not establish evidence-method quality."}},"exam_03_B_case3_q2":{"answer":{"value":92.85714285714286,"unit":"%","abs_tolerance":0.2785714285714286},"rubric":{},"explanation":{"fr":"1. Couverture exigences = 35/38×100 = 92.1053 %.\n2. Réussite essais = 26/28×100 = 92.8571 %.\n3. Exigences sans preuve approuvée = 3.\n4. Le dénominateur des essais ne remplace pas celui des exigences. L’échec critique doit être traité explicitement, quel que soit le pourcentage.\n\nLes comptes sont fictifs et n’établissent pas la qualité des méthodes de preuve.","en":"1. Requirement coverage = 35/38×100 = 92.1053%.\n2. Test pass rate = 26/28×100 = 92.8571%.\n3. Requirements without approved evidence = 3.\n4. Test and requirement denominators are not interchangeable. Address the critical failure explicitly regardless of percentage.\n\nCounts are fictional and do not establish evidence-method quality."}},"exam_03_B_case3_q3":{"answer":{"value":3,"unit":"exigences","abs_tolerance":0.01},"rubric":{},"explanation":{"fr":"1. Couverture exigences = 35/38×100 = 92.1053 %.\n2. Réussite essais = 26/28×100 = 92.8571 %.\n3. Exigences sans preuve approuvée = 3.\n4. Le dénominateur des essais ne remplace pas celui des exigences. L’échec critique doit être traité explicitement, quel que soit le pourcentage.\n\nLes comptes sont fictifs et n’établissent pas la qualité des méthodes de preuve.","en":"1. Requirement coverage = 35/38×100 = 92.1053%.\n2. Test pass rate = 26/28×100 = 92.8571%.\n3. Requirements without approved evidence = 3.\n4. Test and requirement denominators are not interchangeable. Address the critical failure explicitly regardless of percentage.\n\nCounts are fictional and do not establish evidence-method quality."}},"exam_03_B_case3_decision":{"answer":{"choice_id":"exam_03_B_case3_decision_c1"},"rubric":{},"explanation":{"fr":"Garder visibles l’échec critique, les exigences sans preuve et les configurations ; décider un plan de fermeture. Les comptes sont fictifs et n’établissent pas la qualité des méthodes de preuve.","en":"Keep the critical failure, unproven requirements and configurations visible; decide a closure plan. Counts are fictional and do not establish evidence-method quality."}}}'::jsonb) ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
