 prouve pas la date finale.\n\nLe forecast suppose la poursuite de l’efficacité de coût observée.","en":"1. CPI = 104000/135000 = 0.7704.\n2. SPI = 104000/125000 = 0.832.\n3. EAC = 600000/0.7704 ≈ €778846.1538.\n4. CPI < 1 indicates earned work cost more than its budget; SPI does not establish completion date.\n\nForecast assumes observed cost efficiency continues."}},"exam_04_B_case1_decision":{"answer":{"choice_id":"exam_04_B_case1_decision_c2"},"rubric":{},"explanation":{"fr":"Analyser les livrables acquis, le chemin critique et l’hypothèse de forecast avant de décider. Le forecast suppose la poursuite de l’efficacité de coût observée.","en":"Examine earned deliverables, critical path and forecast assumptions before deciding. Forecast assumes observed cost efficiency continues."}},"exam_04_B_case2_q1":{"answer":{"value":47200,"unit":"€","abs_tolerance":141.6},"rubric":{},"explanation":{"fr":"1. Récurrent = 1200×16 = 19200 €.\n2. Fixe = 18000+7000+3000 = 28000 €.\n3. Impact total = 47200 €.\n4. Impact moyen sur population = 39.3333 €/véhicule ; ce n’est pas le nouveau coût récurrent.\n5. Impact exigences, interfaces et preuves reste à analyser.\n\nPas de coût délai ni de retour terrain inclus ; annoncer clairement ces exclusions.","en":"1. Recurring = 1200×16 = €19200.\n2. Fixed = 18000+7000+3000 = €28000.\n3. Total impact = €47200.\n4. Average population impact = €39.3333/vehicle, not the new recurring cost.\n5. Requirement, interface and evidence impacts still need analysis.\n\nSchedule and field-return costs are excluded and must be declared."}},"exam_04_B_case2_q2":{"answer":{"value":39.333333333333336,"unit":"€/véhicule","abs_tolerance":0.11800000000000001},"rubric":{},"explanation":{"fr":"1. Récurrent = 1200×16 = 19200 €.\n2. Fixe = 18000+7000+3000 = 28000 €.\n3. Impact total = 47200 €.\n4. Impact moyen sur population = 39.3333 €/véhicule ; ce n’est pas le nouveau coût récurrent.\n5. Impact exigences, interfaces et preuves reste à analyser.\n\nPas de coût délai ni de retour terrain inclus ; annoncer clairement ces exclusions.","en":"1. Recurring = 1200×16 = €19200.\n2. Fixed = 18000+7000+3000 = €28000.\n3. Total impact = €47200.\n4. Average population impact = €39.3333/vehicle, not the new recurring cost.\n5. Requirement, interface and evidence impacts still need analysis.\n\nSchedule and field-return costs are excluded and must be declared."}},"exam_04_B_case2_q3":{"answer":{"value":19200,"unit":"€","abs_tolerance":57.6},"rubric":{},"explanation":{"fr":"1. Récurrent = 1200×16 = 19200 €.\n2. Fixe = 18000+7000+3000 = 28000 €.\n3. Impact total = 47200 €.\n4. Impact moyen sur population = 39.3333 €/véhicule ; ce n’est pas le nouveau coût récurrent.\n5. Impact exigences, interfaces et preuves reste à analyser.\n\nPas de coût délai ni de retour terrain inclus ; annoncer clairement ces exclusions.","en":"1. Recurring = 1200×16 = €19200.\n2. Fixed = 18000+7000+3000 = €28000.\n3. Total impact = €47200.\n4. Average population impact = €39.3333/vehicle, not the new recurring cost.\n5. Requirement, interface and evidence impacts still need analysis.\n\nSchedule and field-return costs are excluded and must be declared."}},"exam_04_B_case2_decision":{"answer":{"choice_id":"exam_04_B_case2_decision_c1"},"rubric":{},"explanation":{"fr":"Décider après analyse technique, puis fixer effectivité, non-régression et fermeture documentée. Pas de coût délai ni de retour terrain inclus ; annoncer clairement ces exclusions.","en":"Decide after technical analysis, then set effectivity, regression evidence and documented closure. Schedule and field-return costs are excluded and must be declared."}},"exam_04_B_case3_q1":{"answer":{"value":390000,"unit":"€","abs_tolerance":1170.0},"rubric":{},"explanation":{"fr":"1. Total A = 30000+120×3000 = 390000 €.\n2. Total B = 80000+105×3000 = 395000 €.\n3. Croisement = (80000−30000)/(120−105) = 3333.3333 unités.\n4. Le choix économique s’inverse autour de ce seuil si les autres hypothèses tiennent.\n\nService, garantie et délai sont exclus ; les hypothèses d’admissibilité doivent être vérifiées.","en":"1. A total = 30000+120×3000 = €390000.\n2. B total = 80000+105×3000 = €395000.\n3. Break-even = (80000−30000)/(120−105) = 3333.3333 units.\n4. Economic ranking reverses around this threshold if other assumptions hold.\n\nService, warranty and schedule costs are excluded; feasibility assumptions need verification."}},"exam_04_B_case3_q2":{"answer":{"value":395000,"unit":"€","abs_tolerance":1185.0},"rubric":{},"explanation":{"fr":"1. Total A = 30000+120×3000 = 390000 €.\n2. Total B = 80000+105×3000 = 395000 €.\n3. Croisement = (80000−30000)/(120−105) = 3333.3333 unités.\n4. Le choix économique s’inverse autour de ce seuil si les autres hypothèses tiennent.\n\nService, garantie et délai sont exclus ; les hypothèses d’admissibilité doivent être vérifiées.","en":"1. A total = 30000+120×3000 = €390000.\n2. B total = 80000+105×3000 = €395000.\n3. Break-even = (80000−30000)/(120−105) = 3333.3333 units.\n4. Economic ranking reverses around this threshold if other assumptions hold.\n\nService, warranty and schedule costs are excluded; feasibility assumptions need verification."}},"exam_04_B_case3_q3":{"answer":{"value":3333.3333333333335,"unit":"unités","abs_tolerance":0.01},"rubric":{},"explanation":{"fr":"1. Total A = 30000+120×3000 = 390000 €.\n2. Total B = 80000+105×3000 = 395000 €.\n3. Croisement = (80000−30000)/(120−105) = 3333.3333 unités.\n4. Le choix économique s’inverse autour de ce seuil si les autres hypothèses tiennent.\n\nService, garantie et délai sont exclus ; les hypothèses d’admissibilité doivent être vérifiées.","en":"1. A total = 30000+120×3000 = €390000.\n2. B total = 80000+105×3000 = €395000.\n3. Break-even = (80000−30000)/(120−105) = 3333.3333 units.\n4. Economic ranking reverses around this threshold if other assumptions hold.\n\nService, warranty and schedule costs are excluded; feasibility assumptions need verification."}},"exam_04_B_case3_decision":{"answer":{"choice_id":"exam_04_B_case3_decision_c3"},"rubric":{},"explanation":{"fr":"Vérifier volume, délai, capacité, qualité et coûts exclus avant de retenir le coût total le plus faible. Service, garantie et délai sont exclus ; les hypothèses d’admissibilité doivent être vérifiées.","en":"Check volume, schedule, capacity, quality and excluded costs before choosing the lower total. Service, warranty and schedule costs are excluded; feasibility assumptions need verification."}}}'::jsonb) ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.module_exams (id,module_id,threshold,revision) VALUES ('exam_05','module_05',80,1) ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO autoquest_private.exam_forms (exam_id,form,questions,solutions) VALUES ('exam_05','A','[{"id":"exam_05_A_case1_q1","lessonId":"","position":1,"kind":"numeric","points":0,"required":true,"revision":1,"prompt":{"fr":"Pertes à transporter 2000 W ; liquide avec cp = 4 180 J/(kg·K) ; hausse admissible 5 K. Second cas : pertes +20 %. Troisième cas : débit nominal réduit de 20 %, pertes initiales.\n\nCalcule le débit nominal.","en":"Heat to carry 2000 W; coolant cp = 4,180 J/(kg·K); allowed rise 5 K. Second case: heat +20%. Third case: nominal flow reduced by 20%, original heat.\n\nCalculate nominal flow."},"choices":[],"settings":{"unit":"kg/s","toleranceLabel":{"fr":"Tolérance absolue ±0.000287081 kg/s.","en":"Absolute tolerance ±0.000287081 kg/s."}},"blockId":"exam_05_A_case1"},{"id":"exam_05_A_case1_q2","lessonId":"","position":2,"kind":"numeric","points":0,"required":true,"revision":1,"prompt":{"fr":"Pertes à transporter 2000 W ; liquide avec cp = 4 180 J/(kg·K) ; hausse admissible 5 K. Second cas : pertes +20 %. Troisième cas : débit nominal réduit de 20 %, pertes initiales.\n\nCalcule le débit pour pertes +20 %.","en":"Heat to carry 2000 W; coolant cp = 4,180 J/(kg·K); allowed rise 5 K. Second case: heat +20%. Third case: nominal flow reduced by 20%, original heat.\n\nCalculate flow for heat +20%."},"choices":[],"settings":{"unit":"kg/s","toleranceLabel":{"fr":"Tolérance absolue ±0.000344498 kg/s.","en":"Absolute tolerance ±0.000344498 kg/s."}},"blockId":"exam_05_A_case1"},{"id":"exam_05_A_case1_q3","lessonId":"","position":3,"kind":"numeric","points":0,"required":true,"revision":1,"prompt":{"fr":"Pertes à transporter 2000 W ; liquide avec cp = 4 180 J/(kg·K) ; hausse admissible 5 K. Second cas : pertes +20 %. Troisième cas : débit nominal réduit de 20 %, pertes initiales.\n\nCalcule ΔT à débit nominal −20 %.","en":"Heat to carry 2000 W; coolant cp = 4,180 J/(kg·K); allowed rise 5 K. Second case: heat +20%. Third case: nominal flow reduced by 20%, original heat.\n\nCalculate ΔT at nominal flow −20%."},"choices":[],"settings":{"unit":"K","toleranceLabel":{"fr":"Tolérance absolue ±0.02 K.","en":"Absolute tolerance ±0.02 K."}},"blockId":"exam_05_A_case1"},{"id":"exam_05_A_case1_decision","lessonId":"","position":4,"kind":"single_choice","points":0,"required":true,"revision":1,"prompt":{"fr":"Pertes à transporter 2000 W ; liquide avec cp = 4 180 J/(kg·K) ; hausse admissible 5 K. Second cas : pertes +20 %. Troisième cas : débit nominal réduit de 20 %, pertes initiales.\n\nRevue technique : quelle décision est défendable avec les données et les limites du cas ?","en":"Heat to carry 2000 W; coolant cp = 4,180 J/(kg·K); allowed rise 5 K. Second case: heat +20%. Third case: nominal flow reduced by 20%, original heat.\n\nTechnical review: which decision is defensible given the case data and limitations?"},"choices":[{"id":"exam_05_A_case1_decision_c1","position":1,"labels":{"fr":"Réduire le débit de 20 % et annoncer aussi une réduction de ΔT de 20 %.","en":"Reduce flow by 20% and claim ΔT also falls by 20%."}},{"id":"exam_05_A_case1_decision_c2","position":2,"labels":{"fr":"Partager un contrat thermique avec températures, débit, pertes et scénarios, puis vérifier l’échangeur et la pompe.","en":"Share a thermal contract with temperatures, flow, heat and scenarios, then verify exchanger and pump."}},{"id":"exam_05_A_case1_decision_c3","position":3,"labels":{"fr":"Valider le refroidissement sur le seul ΔT sans températures absolues ni échangeur.","en":"Approve cooling from ΔT alone without absolute temperatures or exchanger checks."}}],"settings":{},"blockId":"exam_05_A_case1"},{"id":"exam_05_A_case2_q1","lessonId":"","position":5,"kind":"numeric","points":0,"required":true,"revision":1,"prompt":{"fr":"Charge idéale 156 W sous 12 V au point de calcul ; résistance aller-retour de faisceau 0,05 Ω. Utiliser I = P/12 sans boucle de correction de tension.\n\nCalcule le courant au point imposé.","en":"Ideal load 156 W at a 12 V calculation point; round-trip harness resistance 0.05 Ω. Use I = P/12 without iterative voltage correction.\n\nCalculate current at the stated point."},"choices":[],"settings":{"unit":"A","toleranceLabel":{"fr":"Tolérance absolue ±0.039 A.","en":"Absolute tolerance ±0.039 A."}},"blockId":"exam_05_A_case2"},{"id":"exam_05_A_case2_q2","lessonId":"","position":6,"kind":"numeric","points":0,"required":true,"revision":1,"prompt":{"fr":"Charge idéale 156 W sous 12 V au point de calcul ; résistance aller-retour de faisceau 0,05 Ω. Utiliser I = P/12 sans boucle de correction de tension.\n\nCalcule la chute aller-retour.","en":"Ideal load 156 W at a 12 V calculation point; round-trip harness resistance 0.05 Ω. Use I = P/12 without iterative voltage correction.\n\nCalculate round-trip voltage drop."},"choices":[],"settings":{"unit":"V","toleranceLabel":{"fr":"Tolérance absolue ±0.02 V.","en":"Absolute tolerance ±0.02 V."}},"blockId":"exam_05_A_case2"},{"id":"exam_05_A_case2_q3","lessonId":"","position":7,"kind":"numeric","points":0,"required":true,"revision":1,"prompt":{"fr":"Charge idéale 156 W sous 12 V au point de calcul ; résistance aller-retour de faisceau 0,05 Ω. Utiliser I = P/12 sans boucle de correction de tension.\n\nCalcule les pertes Joule.","en":"Ideal load 156 W at a 12 V calculation point; round-trip harness resistance 0.05 Ω. Use I = P/12 without iterative voltage correction.\n\nCalculate Joule losses."},"choices":[],"settings":{"unit":"W","toleranceLabel":{"fr":"Tolérance absolue ±0.02535 W.","en":"Absolute tolerance ±0.02535 W."}},"blockId":"exam_05_A_case2"},{"id":"exam_05_A_case2_decision","lessonId":"","position":8,"kind":"single_choice","points":0,"required":true,"revision":1,"prompt":{"fr":"Charge idéale 156 W sous 12 V au point de calcul ; résistance aller-retour de faisceau 0,05 Ω. Utiliser I = P/12 sans boucle de correction de tension.\n\nRevue technique : quelle décision est défendable avec les données et les limites du cas ?","en":"Ideal load 156 W at a 12 V calculation point; round-trip harness resistance 0.05 Ω. Use I = P/12 without iterative voltage correction.\n\nTechnical review: which decision is defensible given the case data and limitations?"},"choices":[{"id":"exam_05_A_case2_decision_c1","position":1,"labels":{"fr":"Inclure le retour de masse, les transitoires et la coordination des protections avant de figer le faisceau.","en":"Include ground return, transients and protection coordination before freezing the harness."}},{"id":"exam_05_A_case2_decision_c2","position":2,"labels":{"fr":"Choisir le fusible uniquement avec le courant nominal, sans caractéristique ni courant de défaut.","en":"Select a fuse solely by nominal current without characteristics or fault current."}},{"id":"exam_05_A_case2_decision_c3","position":3,"labels":{"fr":"Oublier le retour parce que la caisse est conductrice.","en":"Ignore the return because the body is conductive."}}],"settings":{},"blockId":"exam_05_A_case2"},{"id":"exam_05_A_case3_q1","lessonId":"","position":9,"kind":"numeric","points":0,"required":true,"revision":1,"prompt":{"fr":"Batterie brute 32 kWh ; fenêtre utile 80 % ; consommation nominale 172 Wh/km, scénario dégradé 192 Wh/km ; cible 150 km.\n\nCalcule l’autonomie nominale.","en":"Gross battery 32 kWh; usable window 80%; nominal consumption 172 Wh/km, degraded case 192 Wh/km; target 150 km.\n\nCalculate nominal range."},"choices":[],"settings":{"unit":"km","toleranceLabel":{"fr":"Tolérance absolue ±0.446512 km.","en":"Absolute tolerance ±0.446512 km."}},"blockId":"exam_05_A_case3"},{"id":"exam_05_A_case3_q2","lessonId":"","position":10,"kind":"numeric","points":0,"required":true,"revision":1,"prompt":{"fr":"Batterie brute 32 kWh ; fenêtre utile 80 % ; consommation nominale 172 Wh/km, scénario dégradé 192 Wh/km ; cible 150 km.\n\nCalcule l’autonomie dans le scénario dégradé.","en":"Gross battery 32 kWh; usable window 80%; nominal consumption 172 Wh/km, degraded case 192 Wh/km; target 150 km.\n\nCalculate degraded-case range."},"choices":[],"settings":{"unit":"km","toleranceLabel":{"fr":"Tolérance absolue ±0.4 km.","en":"Absolute tolerance ±0.4 km."}},"blockId":"exam_05_A_case3"},{"id":"exam_05_A_case3_q3","lessonId":"","position":11,"kind":"numeric","points":0,"required":true,"revision":1,"prompt":{"fr":"Batterie brute 32 kWh ; fenêtre utile 80 % ; consommation nominale 172 Wh/km, scénario dégradé 192 Wh/km ; cible 150 km.\n\nCalcule l’énergie utile nécessaire pour 150 km dégradés.","en":"Gross battery 32 kWh; usable window 80%; nominal consumption 172 Wh/km, degraded case 192 Wh/km; target 150 km.\n\nCalculate usable energy needed for 150 degraded kilometres."},"choices":[],"settings":{"unit":"kWh","toleranceLabel":{"fr":"Tolérance absolue ±0.0864 kWh.","en":"Absolute tolerance ±0.0864 kWh."}},"blockId":"exam_05_A_case3"},{"id":"exam_05_A_case3_decision","lessonId":"","position":12,"kind":"single_choice","points":0,"required":true,"revision":1,"prompt":{"fr":"Batterie brute 32 kWh ; fenêtre utile 80 % ; consommation nominale 172 Wh/km, scénario dégradé 192 Wh/km ; cible 150 km.\n\nRevue technique : quelle décision est défendable avec les données et les limites du cas ?","en":"Gross battery 32 kWh; usable window 80%; nominal consumption 172 Wh/km, degraded case 192 Wh/km; target 150 km.\n\nTechnical review: which decision is defensible given the case data and limitations?"},"choices":[{"id":"exam_05_A_case3_decision_c1","position":1,"labels":{"fr":"Utiliser l’énergie brute pour tous les scénarios, puisque la fenêtre ne change que la recharge.","en":"Use gross energy in every scenario because the window only affects charging."}},{"id":"exam_05_A_case3_decision_c2","position":2,"labels":{"fr":"Moyenner les deux autonomies pour déclarer la cible satisfaite dans les deux cas.","en":"Average both ranges to declare that both scenarios meet the target."}},{"id":"exam_05_A_case3_decision_c3","position":3,"labels":{"fr":"Conserver deux verdicts conditionnels et étudier masse, thermique et consommation avant d’augmenter la batterie.","en":"Keep separate conditional verdicts and examine mass, thermal limits and consumption before increasing battery capacity."}}],"settings":{},"blockId":"exam_05_A_case3"}]'::jsonb,'{"exam_05_A_case1_q1":{"answer":{"value":0.09569377990430622,"unit":"kg/s","abs_tolerance":0.00028708133971291867},"rubric":{},"explanation":{"fr":"1. Débit nominal = 2000/(4180×5) = 0.0957 kg/s.\n2. Pertes +20 % : débit nécessaire 0.1148 kg/s.\n3. Débit −20 % : hausse = 5/0,8 = 6.25 K.\n4. Vérifier ensuite températures d’entrée, pompe, échangeur et perte de charge.\n\nChaleur spécifique constante et régime établi, sans modèle d’échangeur.","en":"1. Nominal flow = 2000/(4180×5) = 0.0957 kg/s.\n2. Heat +20%: required flow 0.1148 kg/s.\n3. Flow −20%: rise = 5/0.8 = 6.25 K.\n4. Then check inlet temperatures, pump, heat exchanger and pressure loss.\n\nConstant heat capacity and steady state, without an exchanger model."}},"exam_05_A_case1_q2":{"answer":{"value":0.11483253588516747,"unit":"kg/s","abs_tolerance":0.0003444976076555024},"rubric":{},"explanation":{"fr":"1. Débit nominal = 2000/(4180×5) = 0.0957 kg/s.\n2. Pertes +20 % : débit nécessaire 0.1148 kg/s.\n3. Débit −20 % : hausse = 5/0,8 = 6.25 K.\n4. Vérifier ensuite températures d’entrée, pompe, échangeur et perte de charge.\n\nChaleur spécifique constante et régime établi, sans modèle d’échangeur.","en":"1. Nominal flow = 2000/(4180×5) = 0.0957 kg/s.\n2. Heat +20%: required flow 0.1148 kg/s.\n3. Flow −20%: rise = 5/0.8 = 6.25 K.\n4. Then check inlet temperatures, pump, heat exchanger and pressure loss.\n\nConstant heat capacity and steady state, without an exchanger model."}},"exam_05_A_case1_q3":{"answer":{"value":6.249999999999999,"unit":"K","abs_tolerance":0.02},"rubric":{},"explanation":{"fr":"1. Débit nominal = 2000/(4180×5) = 0.0957 kg/s.\n2. Pertes +20 % : débit nécessaire 0.1148 kg/s.\n3. Débit −20 % : hausse = 5/0,8 = 6.25 K.\n4. Vérifier ensuite températures d’entrée, pompe, échangeur et perte de charge.\n\nChaleur spécifique constante et régime établi, sans modèle d’échangeur.","en":"1. Nominal flow = 2000/(4180×5) = 0.0957 kg/s.\n2. Heat +20%: required flow 0.1148 kg/s.\n3. Flow −20%: rise = 5/0.8 = 6.25 K.\n4. Then check inlet temperatures, pump, heat exchanger and pressure loss.\n\nConstant heat capacity and steady state, without an exchanger model."}},"exam_05_A_case1_decision":{"answer":{"choice_id":"exam_05_A_case1_decision_c2"},"rubric":{},"explanation":{"fr":"Partager un contrat thermique avec températures, débit, pertes et scénarios, puis vérifier l’échangeur et la pompe. Chaleur spécifique constante et régime établi, sans modèle d’échangeur.","en":"Share a thermal contract with temperatures, flow, heat and scenarios, then verify exchanger and pump. Constant heat capacity and steady state, without an exchanger model."}},"exam_05_A_case2_q1":{"answer":{"value":13.0,"unit":"A","abs_tolerance":0.039},"rubric":{},"explanation":{"fr":"1. I = 156/12 = 13 A.\n2. Chute = 13×0,05 = 0.65 V.\n3. Pertes = 13²×0,05 = 8.45 W.\n4. La tension réelle et le comportement de charge demandent un modèle couplé pour affiner.\n\nLe calcul fixe la tension pour une première estimation ; la charge peut réagir à la chute réelle.","en":"1. I = 156/12 = 13 A.\n2. Drop = 13×0.05 = 0.65 V.\n3. Loss = 13²×0.05 = 8.45 W.\n4. Actual voltage and load behaviour need a coupled model for refinement.\n\nVoltage is fixed for an initial estimate; the load may respond to actual drop."}},"exam_05_A_case2_q2":{"answer":{"value":0.65,"unit":"V","abs_tolerance":0.02},"rubric":{},"explanation":{"fr":"1. I = 156/12 = 13 A.\n2. Chute = 13×0,05 = 0.65 V.\n3. Pertes = 13²×0,05 = 8.45 W.\n4. La tension réelle et le comportement de charge demandent un modèle couplé pour affiner.\n\nLe calcul fixe la tension pour une première estimation ; la charge peut réagir à la chute réelle.","en":"1. I = 156/12 = 13 A.\n2. Drop = 13×0.05 = 0.65 V.\n3. Loss = 13²×0.05 = 8.45 W.\n4. Actual voltage and load behaviour need a coupled model for refinement.\n\nVoltage is fixed for an initial estimate; the load may respond to actual drop."}},"exam_05_A_case2_q3":{"answer":{"value":8.450000000000001,"unit":"W","abs_tolerance":0.025350000000000004},"rubric":{},"explanation":{"fr":"1. I = 156/12 = 13 A.\n2. Chute = 13×0,05 = 0.65 V.\n3. Pertes = 13²×0,05 = 8.45 W.\n4. La tension réelle et le comportement de charge demandent un modèle couplé pour affiner.\n\nLe calcul fixe la tension pour une première estimation ; la charge peut réagir à la chute réelle.","en":"1. I = 156/12 = 13 A.\n2. Drop = 13×0.05 = 0.65 V.\n3. Loss = 13²×0.05 = 8.45 W.\n4. Actual voltage and load behaviour need a coupled model for refinement.\n\nVoltage is fixed for an initial estimate; the load may respond to actual drop."}},"exam_05_A_case2_decision":{"answer":{"choice_id":"exam_05_A_case2_decision_c1"},"rubric":{},"explanation":{"fr":"Inclure le retour de masse, les transitoires et la coordination des protections avant de figer le faisceau. Le calcul fixe la tension pour une première estimation ; la charge peut réagir à la chute réelle.","en":"Include ground return, transients and protection coordination before freezing the harness. Voltage is fixed for an initial estimate; the load may respond to actual drop."}},"exam_05_A_case3_q1":{"answer":{"value":148.8372093023256,"unit":"km","abs_tolerance":0.4465116279069768},"rubric":{},"explanation":{"fr":"1. Énergie utile : 32 × 0,80 = 25.6 kWh.\n2. Convertir en Wh : 25600 Wh.\n3. Autonomie nominale : 25600 / 172 = 148.8372 km.\n4. Autonomie dégradée : 25600 / 192 = 133.3333 km.\n5. Besoin utile pour 150 km dégradés : 150 × 192/1000 = 28.8 kWh. Comparer séparément chaque scénario à 150 km.\n\nLa consommation est supposée constante et indépendante de la masse ; le résultat ne prouve pas une autonomie sur cycle réel.","en":"1. Usable energy: 32 × 0.80 = 25.6 kWh.\n2. Convert to Wh: 25600 Wh.\n3. Nominal range: 25600 / 172 = 148.8372 km.\n4. Degraded range: 25600 / 192 = 133.3333 km.\n5. Usable energy for 150 degraded kilometres: 150 × 192/1000 = 28.8 kWh. Compare each scenario separately with 150 km.\n\nConsumption is assumed constant and independent of mass; this does not establish actual drive-cycle range."}},"exam_05_A_case3_q2":{"answer":{"value":133.33333333333334,"unit":"km","abs_tolerance":0.4},"rubric":{},"explanation":{"fr":"1. Énergie utile : 32 × 0,80 = 25.6 kWh.\n2. Convertir en Wh : 25600 Wh.\n3. Autonomie nominale : 25600 / 172 = 148.8372 km.\n4. Autonomie dégradée : 25600 / 192 = 133.3333 km.\n5. Besoin utile pour 150 km dégradés : 150 × 192/1000 = 28.8 kWh. Comparer séparément chaque scénario à 150 km.\n\nLa consommation est supposée constante et indépendante de la masse ; le résultat ne prouve pas une autonomie sur cycle réel.","en":"1. Usable energy: 32 × 0.80 = 25.6 kWh.\n2. Convert to Wh: 25600 Wh.\n3. Nominal range: 25600 / 172 = 148.8372 km.\n4. Degraded range: 25600 / 192 = 133.3333 km.\n5. Usable energy for 150 degraded kilometres: 150 × 192/1000 = 28.8 kWh. Compare each scenario separately with 150 km.\n\nConsumption is assumed constant and independent of mass; this does not establish actual drive-cycle range."}},"exam_05_A_case3_q3":{"answer":{"value":28.8,"unit":"kWh","abs_tolerance":0.0864},"rubric":{},"explanation":{"fr":"1. Énergie utile : 32 × 0,80 = 25.6 kWh.\n2. Convertir en Wh : 25600 Wh.\n3. Autonomie nominale : 25600 / 172 = 148.8372 km.\n4. Autonomie dégradée : 25600 / 192 = 133.3333 km.\n5. Besoin utile pour 150 km dégradés : 150 × 192/1000 = 28.8 kWh. Comparer séparément chaque scénario à 150 km.\n\nLa consommation est supposée constante et indépendante de la masse ; le résultat ne prouve pas une autonomie sur cycle réel.","en":"1. Usable energy: 32 × 0.80 = 25.6 kWh.\n2. Convert to Wh: 25600 Wh.\n3. Nominal range: 25600 / 172 = 148.8372 km.\n4. Degraded range: 25600 / 192 = 133.3333 km.\n5. Usable energy for 150 degraded kilometres: 150 × 192/1000 = 28.8 kWh. Compare each scenario separately with 150 km.\n\nConsumption is assumed constant and independent of mass; this does not establish actual drive-cycle range."}},"exam_05_A_case3_decision":{"answer":{"choice_id":"exam_05_A_case3_decision_c3"},"rubric":{},"explanation":{"fr":"Conserver deux verdicts conditionnels et étudier masse, thermique et consommation avant d’augmenter la batterie. La consommation est supposée constante et indépendante de la masse ; le résultat ne prouve pas une autonomie sur cycle réel.","en":"Keep separate conditional verdicts and examine mass, thermal limits and consumption before increasing battery capacity. Consumption is assumed constant and independent of mass; this does not establish actual drive-cycle range."}}}'::jsonb) ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
