; 1520 good without rework; 50 additional units recovered by rework; remainder scrapped. Groups are disjoint.\n\nTechnical review: which decision is defensible given the case data and limitations?"},"choices":[{"id":"exam_07_B_case2_decision_c1","position":1,"labels":{"fr":"Suivre premier passage, retouches et rebuts séparément, puis démontrer une cause avant correction.","en":"Track first pass, rework and scrap separately, then demonstrate a cause before correcting."}},{"id":"exam_07_B_case2_decision_c2","position":2,"labels":{"fr":"Annoncer le rendement final comme FPY et supprimer les retouches du dashboard.","en":"Call final yield FPY and remove rework from the dashboard."}},{"id":"exam_07_B_case2_decision_c3","position":3,"labels":{"fr":"Déclarer la production maîtrisée parce qu’une unité prototype a réussi.","en":"Declare production controlled because one prototype passed."}}],"settings":{},"blockId":"exam_07_B_case2"},{"id":"exam_07_B_case3_q1","lessonId":"","position":9,"kind":"numeric","points":0,"required":true,"revision":1,"prompt":{"fr":"34 exigences applicables ; 31 ont une preuve approuvée ; 26 essais exécutés, dont 24 réussis et 2 échoués. Un échec est critique. Les deux populations sont distinctes.\n\nCalcule la couverture des exigences.","en":"34 applicable requirements; 31 have approved evidence; 26 tests executed, 24 passed and 2 failed. One failure is critical. The populations are distinct.\n\nCalculate requirement coverage."},"choices":[],"settings":{"unit":"%","toleranceLabel":{"fr":"Tolérance absolue ±0.273529 %.","en":"Absolute tolerance ±0.273529 %."}},"blockId":"exam_07_B_case3"},{"id":"exam_07_B_case3_q2","lessonId":"","position":10,"kind":"numeric","points":0,"required":true,"revision":1,"prompt":{"fr":"34 exigences applicables ; 31 ont une preuve approuvée ; 26 essais exécutés, dont 24 réussis et 2 échoués. Un échec est critique. Les deux populations sont distinctes.\n\nCalcule le taux de réussite des essais exécutés.","en":"34 applicable requirements; 31 have approved evidence; 26 tests executed, 24 passed and 2 failed. One failure is critical. The populations are distinct.\n\nCalculate executed-test pass rate."},"choices":[],"settings":{"unit":"%","toleranceLabel":{"fr":"Tolérance absolue ±0.276923 %.","en":"Absolute tolerance ±0.276923 %."}},"blockId":"exam_07_B_case3"},{"id":"exam_07_B_case3_q3","lessonId":"","position":11,"kind":"numeric","points":0,"required":true,"revision":1,"prompt":{"fr":"34 exigences applicables ; 31 ont une preuve approuvée ; 26 essais exécutés, dont 24 réussis et 2 échoués. Un échec est critique. Les deux populations sont distinctes.\n\nCompte les exigences sans preuve approuvée.","en":"34 applicable requirements; 31 have approved evidence; 26 tests executed, 24 passed and 2 failed. One failure is critical. The populations are distinct.\n\nCount requirements without approved evidence."},"choices":[],"settings":{"unit":"exigences","toleranceLabel":{"fr":"Tolérance absolue ±0.01 exigences.","en":"Absolute tolerance ±0.01 exigences."}},"blockId":"exam_07_B_case3"},{"id":"exam_07_B_case3_decision","lessonId":"","position":12,"kind":"single_choice","points":0,"required":true,"revision":1,"prompt":{"fr":"34 exigences applicables ; 31 ont une preuve approuvée ; 26 essais exécutés, dont 24 réussis et 2 échoués. Un échec est critique. Les deux populations sont distinctes.\n\nRevue technique : quelle décision est défendable avec les données et les limites du cas ?","en":"34 applicable requirements; 31 have approved evidence; 26 tests executed, 24 passed and 2 failed. One failure is critical. The populations are distinct.\n\nTechnical review: which decision is defensible given the case data and limitations?"},"choices":[{"id":"exam_07_B_case3_decision_c1","position":1,"labels":{"fr":"Moyenner les deux pourcentages pour annoncer une conformité véhicule unique.","en":"Average the percentages to announce a single vehicle-compliance rate."}},{"id":"exam_07_B_case3_decision_c2","position":2,"labels":{"fr":"Reclasser les deux échecs comme non exécutés pour améliorer le taux.","en":"Reclassify failures as not executed to improve the rate."}},{"id":"exam_07_B_case3_decision_c3","position":3,"labels":{"fr":"Garder visibles l’échec critique, les exigences sans preuve et les configurations ; décider un plan de fermeture.","en":"Keep the critical failure, unproven requirements and configurations visible; decide a closure plan."}}],"settings":{},"blockId":"exam_07_B_case3"}]'::jsonb,'{"exam_07_B_case1_q1":{"answer":{"value":18400.0,"unit":"€/an","abs_tolerance":55.2},"rubric":{},"explanation":{"fr":"1. Exposition avant = 0,08×230000 = 18400 €/an.\n2. Après = 0,03×230000 = 6900 €/an.\n3. Gain net espéré = 18400−6900−5000 = 6500 €/an.\n4. Ce gain dépend d’une réduction de probabilité supposée ; la sécurité exige objectifs, tests et risque résiduel.\n\nLes probabilités d’attaque sont fictives ; aucune décision de conformité réelle n’en découle.","en":"1. Exposure before = 0.08×230000 = €18400/year.\n2. After = 0.03×230000 = €6900/year.\n3. Expected net benefit = 18400−6900−5000 = €6500/year.\n4. Benefit depends on an assumed probability reduction; security needs objectives, tests and residual-risk analysis.\n\nAttack probabilities are fictional; no actual compliance decision follows."}},"exam_07_B_case1_q2":{"answer":{"value":6900.0,"unit":"€/an","abs_tolerance":20.7},"rubric":{},"explanation":{"fr":"1. Exposition avant = 0,08×230000 = 18400 €/an.\n2. Après = 0,03×230000 = 6900 €/an.\n3. Gain net espéré = 18400−6900−5000 = 6500 €/an.\n4. Ce gain dépend d’une réduction de probabilité supposée ; la sécurité exige objectifs, tests et risque résiduel.\n\nLes probabilités d’attaque sont fictives ; aucune décision de conformité réelle n’en découle.","en":"1. Exposure before = 0.08×230000 = €18400/year.\n2. After = 0.03×230000 = €6900/year.\n3. Expected net benefit = 18400−6900−5000 = €6500/year.\n4. Benefit depends on an assumed probability reduction; security needs objectives, tests and residual-risk analysis.\n\nAttack probabilities are fictional; no actual compliance decision follows."}},"exam_07_B_case1_q3":{"answer":{"value":6500.0,"unit":"€/an","abs_tolerance":19.5},"rubric":{},"explanation":{"fr":"1. Exposition avant = 0,08×230000 = 18400 €/an.\n2. Après = 0,03×230000 = 6900 €/an.\n3. Gain net espéré = 18400−6900−5000 = 6500 €/an.\n4. Ce gain dépend d’une réduction de probabilité supposée ; la sécurité exige objectifs, tests et risque résiduel.\n\nLes probabilités d’attaque sont fictives ; aucune décision de conformité réelle n’en découle.","en":"1. Exposure before = 0.08×230000 = €18400/year.\n2. After = 0.03×230000 = €6900/year.\n3. Expected net benefit = 18400−6900−5000 = €6500/year.\n4. Benefit depends on an assumed probability reduction; security needs objectives, tests and residual-risk analysis.\n\nAttack probabilities are fictional; no actual compliance decision follows."}},"exam_07_B_case1_decision":{"answer":{"choice_id":"exam_07_B_case1_decision_c2"},"rubric":{},"explanation":{"fr":"Traiter les probabilités comme hypothèses et vérifier efficacité, autorisation, logs et récupération du contrôle. Les probabilités d’attaque sont fictives ; aucune décision de conformité réelle n’en découle.","en":"Treat probabilities as assumptions and verify control effectiveness, authorisation, logs and recovery. Attack probabilities are fictional; no actual compliance decision follows."}},"exam_07_B_case2_q1":{"answer":{"value":95.0,"unit":"%","abs_tolerance":0.28500000000000003},"rubric":{},"explanation":{"fr":"1. FPY = 1520/1600×100 = 95 %.\n2. Rendement final = (1520+50)/1600×100 = 98.125 %.\n3. Rebuts = 1600−1520−50 = 30.\n4. Les 50 reprises coûtent du temps et des ressources, même si elles sont finalement bonnes.\n\nLe rendement seul ne démontre ni capabilité ni stabilité du procédé.","en":"1. FPY = 1520/1600×100 = 95%.\n2. Final yield = (1520+50)/1600×100 = 98.125%.\n3. Scrap = 1600−1520−50 = 30.\n4. Rework consumes time and resources even when the units ultimately pass.\n\nYield alone establishes neither capability nor process stability."}},"exam_07_B_case2_q2":{"answer":{"value":98.125,"unit":"%","abs_tolerance":0.294375},"rubric":{},"explanation":{"fr":"1. FPY = 1520/1600×100 = 95 %.\n2. Rendement final = (1520+50)/1600×100 = 98.125 %.\n3. Rebuts = 1600−1520−50 = 30.\n4. Les 50 reprises coûtent du temps et des ressources, même si elles sont finalement bonnes.\n\nLe rendement seul ne démontre ni capabilité ni stabilité du procédé.","en":"1. FPY = 1520/1600×100 = 95%.\n2. Final yield = (1520+50)/1600×100 = 98.125%.\n3. Scrap = 1600−1520−50 = 30.\n4. Rework consumes time and resources even when the units ultimately pass.\n\nYield alone establishes neither capability nor process stability."}},"exam_07_B_case2_q3":{"answer":{"value":30,"unit":"unités","abs_tolerance":0.01},"rubric":{},"explanation":{"fr":"1. FPY = 1520/1600×100 = 95 %.\n2. Rendement final = (1520+50)/1600×100 = 98.125 %.\n3. Rebuts = 1600−1520−50 = 30.\n4. Les 50 reprises coûtent du temps et des ressources, même si elles sont finalement bonnes.\n\nLe rendement seul ne démontre ni capabilité ni stabilité du procédé.","en":"1. FPY = 1520/1600×100 = 95%.\n2. Final yield = (1520+50)/1600×100 = 98.125%.\n3. Scrap = 1600−1520−50 = 30.\n4. Rework consumes time and resources even when the units ultimately pass.\n\nYield alone establishes neither capability nor process stability."}},"exam_07_B_case2_decision":{"answer":{"choice_id":"exam_07_B_case2_decision_c1"},"rubric":{},"explanation":{"fr":"Suivre premier passage, retouches et rebuts séparément, puis démontrer une cause avant correction. Le rendement seul ne démontre ni capabilité ni stabilité du procédé.","en":"Track first pass, rework and scrap separately, then demonstrate a cause before correcting. Yield alone establishes neither capability nor process stability."}},"exam_07_B_case3_q1":{"answer":{"value":91.17647058823529,"unit":"%","abs_tolerance":0.27352941176470585},"rubric":{},"explanation":{"fr":"1. Couverture exigences = 31/34×100 = 91.1765 %.\n2. Réussite essais = 24/26×100 = 92.3077 %.\n3. Exigences sans preuve approuvée = 3.\n4. Le dénominateur des essais ne remplace pas celui des exigences. L’échec critique doit être traité explicitement, quel que soit le pourcentage.\n\nLes comptes sont fictifs et n’établissent pas la qualité des méthodes de preuve.","en":"1. Requirement coverage = 31/34×100 = 91.1765%.\n2. Test pass rate = 24/26×100 = 92.3077%.\n3. Requirements without approved evidence = 3.\n4. Test and requirement denominators are not interchangeable. Address the critical failure explicitly regardless of percentage.\n\nCounts are fictional and do not establish evidence-method quality."}},"exam_07_B_case3_q2":{"answer":{"value":92.3076923076923,"unit":"%","abs_tolerance":0.27692307692307694},"rubric":{},"explanation":{"fr":"1. Couverture exigences = 31/34×100 = 91.1765 %.\n2. Réussite essais = 24/26×100 = 92.3077 %.\n3. Exigences sans preuve approuvée = 3.\n4. Le dénominateur des essais ne remplace pas celui des exigences. L’échec critique doit être traité explicitement, quel que soit le pourcentage.\n\nLes comptes sont fictifs et n’établissent pas la qualité des méthodes de preuve.","en":"1. Requirement coverage = 31/34×100 = 91.1765%.\n2. Test pass rate = 24/26×100 = 92.3077%.\n3. Requirements without approved evidence = 3.\n4. Test and requirement denominators are not interchangeable. Address the critical failure explicitly regardless of percentage.\n\nCounts are fictional and do not establish evidence-method quality."}},"exam_07_B_case3_q3":{"answer":{"value":3,"unit":"exigences","abs_tolerance":0.01},"rubric":{},"explanation":{"fr":"1. Couverture exigences = 31/34×100 = 91.1765 %.\n2. Réussite essais = 24/26×100 = 92.3077 %.\n3. Exigences sans preuve approuvée = 3.\n4. Le dénominateur des essais ne remplace pas celui des exigences. L’échec critique doit être traité explicitement, quel que soit le pourcentage.\n\nLes comptes sont fictifs et n’établissent pas la qualité des méthodes de preuve.","en":"1. Requirement coverage = 31/34×100 = 91.1765%.\n2. Test pass rate = 24/26×100 = 92.3077%.\n3. Requirements without approved evidence = 3.\n4. Test and requirement denominators are not interchangeable. Address the critical failure explicitly regardless of percentage.\n\nCounts are fictional and do not establish evidence-method quality."}},"exam_07_B_case3_decision":{"answer":{"choice_id":"exam_07_B_case3_decision_c3"},"rubric":{},"explanation":{"fr":"Garder visibles l’échec critique, les exigences sans preuve et les configurations ; décider un plan de fermeture. Les comptes sont fictifs et n’établissent pas la qualité des méthodes de preuve.","en":"Keep the critical failure, unproven requirements and configurations visible; decide a closure plan. Counts are fictional and do not establish evidence-method quality."}}}'::jsonb) ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
