ssume constant future CPI.\n\nTechnical review: which decision is defensible given the case data and limitations?"},"choices":[{"id":"exam_08_B_case2_decision_c1","position":1,"labels":{"fr":"Déclarer le programme techniquement validé parce que EV est positif.","en":"Declare technical validation because EV is positive."}},{"id":"exam_08_B_case2_decision_c2","position":2,"labels":{"fr":"Utiliser SPI comme facteur de conversion certain vers une date de fin.","en":"Use SPI as a certain conversion factor to a completion date."}},{"id":"exam_08_B_case2_decision_c3","position":3,"labels":{"fr":"Analyser les livrables acquis, le chemin critique et l’hypothèse de forecast avant de décider.","en":"Examine earned deliverables, critical path and forecast assumptions before deciding."}}],"settings":{},"blockId":"exam_08_B_case2"},{"id":"exam_08_B_case3_q1","lessonId":"","position":9,"kind":"numeric","points":0,"required":true,"revision":1,"prompt":{"fr":"Demande de couple 20 N·m ; codage entier non signé uint16, résolution 0,1 N·m/bit, offset zéro, little-endian. Le décodage inversé utilise aussi uint16.\n\nCalcule la valeur entière brute.","en":"Torque demand 20 N·m; unsigned uint16 integer, resolution 0.1 N·m/bit, zero offset, little-endian. Reversed decoding also uses uint16.\n\nCalculate raw integer value."},"choices":[],"settings":{"unit":"code","toleranceLabel":{"fr":"Tolérance absolue ±0.01 code.","en":"Absolute tolerance ±0.01 code."}},"blockId":"exam_08_B_case3"},{"id":"exam_08_B_case3_q2","lessonId":"","position":10,"kind":"numeric","points":0,"required":true,"revision":1,"prompt":{"fr":"Demande de couple 20 N·m ; codage entier non signé uint16, résolution 0,1 N·m/bit, offset zéro, little-endian. Le décodage inversé utilise aussi uint16.\n\nCalcule le couple obtenu par lecture inversée.","en":"Torque demand 20 N·m; unsigned uint16 integer, resolution 0.1 N·m/bit, zero offset, little-endian. Reversed decoding also uses uint16.\n\nCalculate torque after reversed-byte decoding."},"choices":[],"settings":{"unit":"N·m","toleranceLabel":{"fr":"Tolérance absolue ±15.36 N·m.","en":"Absolute tolerance ±15.36 N·m."}},"blockId":"exam_08_B_case3"},{"id":"exam_08_B_case3_q3","lessonId":"","position":11,"kind":"numeric","points":0,"required":true,"revision":1,"prompt":{"fr":"Demande de couple 20 N·m ; codage entier non signé uint16, résolution 0,1 N·m/bit, offset zéro, little-endian. Le décodage inversé utilise aussi uint16.\n\nDonne la valeur décimale du premier octet transmis.","en":"Torque demand 20 N·m; unsigned uint16 integer, resolution 0.1 N·m/bit, zero offset, little-endian. Reversed decoding also uses uint16.\n\nGive the decimal value of the first transmitted byte."},"choices":[],"settings":{"unit":"octet","toleranceLabel":{"fr":"Tolérance absolue ±0.01 octet.","en":"Absolute tolerance ±0.01 octet."}},"blockId":"exam_08_B_case3"},{"id":"exam_08_B_case3_decision","lessonId":"","position":12,"kind":"single_choice","points":0,"required":true,"revision":1,"prompt":{"fr":"Demande de couple 20 N·m ; codage entier non signé uint16, résolution 0,1 N·m/bit, offset zéro, little-endian. Le décodage inversé utilise aussi uint16.\n\nRevue technique : quelle décision est défendable avec les données et les limites du cas ?","en":"Torque demand 20 N·m; unsigned uint16 integer, resolution 0.1 N·m/bit, zero offset, little-endian. Reversed decoding also uses uint16.\n\nTechnical review: which decision is defensible given the case data and limitations?"},"choices":[{"id":"exam_08_B_case3_decision_c1","position":1,"labels":{"fr":"Accepter l’échange parce que les deux équipements sont conformes à leurs spécifications locales.","en":"Accept the exchange because both devices meet their local specifications."}},{"id":"exam_08_B_case3_decision_c2","position":2,"labels":{"fr":"Fixer et tester unité, signe, ordre des octets, domaine et réaction au défaut dans l’ICD.","en":"Specify and test unit, sign, byte order, range and fault response in the ICD."}},{"id":"exam_08_B_case3_decision_c3","position":3,"labels":{"fr":"Corriger par un gain de calibration sans modifier le contrat d’interface ni tester les limites.","en":"Apply a calibration gain without fixing the interface contract or testing limits."}}],"settings":{},"blockId":"exam_08_B_case3"}]'::jsonb,'{"exam_08_B_case1_q1":{"answer":{"value":100800.0,"unit":"€","abs_tolerance":302.40000000000003},"rubric":{},"explanation":{"fr":"1. Gain brut = 24000×4.2 = 100800 €.\n2. Gain net simple = 100800−25000 = 75800 €.\n3. Volume de retour simple = 25000/4.2 = 5952.381 unités.\n4. Vérifier durabilité, assemblage, service et effectivité avant de comptabiliser le gain comme acquis.\n\nPas d’actualisation, de coût délai ou de variation de taux de rebut dans ce premier calcul.","en":"1. Gross saving = 24000×4.2 = €100800.\n2. Simple net saving = 100800−25000 = €75800.\n3. Simple break-even volume = 25000/4.2 = 5952.381 units.\n4. Verify durability, assembly, service and effectivity before recognising realised savings.\n\nNo discounting, schedule cost or scrap-rate changes in this initial calculation."}},"exam_08_B_case1_q2":{"answer":{"value":75800.0,"unit":"€","abs_tolerance":227.4},"rubric":{},"explanation":{"fr":"1. Gain brut = 24000×4.2 = 100800 €.\n2. Gain net simple = 100800−25000 = 75800 €.\n3. Volume de retour simple = 25000/4.2 = 5952.381 unités.\n4. Vérifier durabilité, assemblage, service et effectivité avant de comptabiliser le gain comme acquis.\n\nPas d’actualisation, de coût délai ou de variation de taux de rebut dans ce premier calcul.","en":"1. Gross saving = 24000×4.2 = €100800.\n2. Simple net saving = 100800−25000 = €75800.\n3. Simple break-even volume = 25000/4.2 = 5952.381 units.\n4. Verify durability, assembly, service and effectivity before recognising realised savings.\n\nNo discounting, schedule cost or scrap-rate changes in this initial calculation."}},"exam_08_B_case1_q3":{"answer":{"value":5952.380952380952,"unit":"unités","abs_tolerance":0.01},"rubric":{},"explanation":{"fr":"1. Gain brut = 24000×4.2 = 100800 €.\n2. Gain net simple = 100800−25000 = 75800 €.\n3. Volume de retour simple = 25000/4.2 = 5952.381 unités.\n4. Vérifier durabilité, assemblage, service et effectivité avant de comptabiliser le gain comme acquis.\n\nPas d’actualisation, de coût délai ou de variation de taux de rebut dans ce premier calcul.","en":"1. Gross saving = 24000×4.2 = €100800.\n2. Simple net saving = 100800−25000 = €75800.\n3. Simple break-even volume = 25000/4.2 = 5952.381 units.\n4. Verify durability, assembly, service and effectivity before recognising realised savings.\n\nNo discounting, schedule cost or scrap-rate changes in this initial calculation."}},"exam_08_B_case1_decision":{"answer":{"choice_id":"exam_08_B_case1_decision_c1"},"rubric":{},"explanation":{"fr":"Valider les fonctions et les interfaces après modification, puis mesurer l’économie sur la population effective. Pas d’actualisation, de coût délai ou de variation de taux de rebut dans ce premier calcul.","en":"Validate functions and interfaces after change, then measure savings on the effective population. No discounting, schedule cost or scrap-rate changes in this initial calculation."}},"exam_08_B_case2_q1":{"answer":{"value":0.7714285714285715,"unit":"ratio","abs_tolerance":0.0023142857142857145},"rubric":{},"explanation":{"fr":"1. CPI = 108000/140000 = 0.7714.\n2. SPI = 108000/130000 = 0.8308.\n3. EAC = 600000/0.7714 ≈ 777777.7778 €.\n4. CPI < 1 indique un coût supérieur au budget de la valeur acquise ; SPI ne prouve pas la date finale.\n\nLe forecast suppose la poursuite de l’efficacité de coût observée.","en":"1. CPI = 108000/140000 = 0.7714.\n2. SPI = 108000/130000 = 0.8308.\n3. EAC = 600000/0.7714 ≈ €777777.7778.\n4. CPI < 1 indicates earned work cost more than its budget; SPI does not establish completion date.\n\nForecast assumes observed cost efficiency continues."}},"exam_08_B_case2_q2":{"answer":{"value":0.8307692307692308,"unit":"ratio","abs_tolerance":0.0024923076923076925},"rubric":{},"explanation":{"fr":"1. CPI = 108000/140000 = 0.7714.\n2. SPI = 108000/130000 = 0.8308.\n3. EAC = 600000/0.7714 ≈ 777777.7778 €.\n4. CPI < 1 indique un coût supérieur au budget de la valeur acquise ; SPI ne prouve pas la date finale.\n\nLe forecast suppose la poursuite de l’efficacité de coût observée.","en":"1. CPI = 108000/140000 = 0.7714.\n2. SPI = 108000/130000 = 0.8308.\n3. EAC = 600000/0.7714 ≈ €777777.7778.\n4. CPI < 1 indicates earned work cost more than its budget; SPI does not establish completion date.\n\nForecast assumes observed cost efficiency continues."}},"exam_08_B_case2_q3":{"answer":{"value":777777.7777777778,"unit":"€","abs_tolerance":2333.3333333333335},"rubric":{},"explanation":{"fr":"1. CPI = 108000/140000 = 0.7714.\n2. SPI = 108000/130000 = 0.8308.\n3. EAC = 600000/0.7714 ≈ 777777.7778 €.\n4. CPI < 1 indique un coût supérieur au budget de la valeur acquise ; SPI ne prouve pas la date finale.\n\nLe forecast suppose la poursuite de l’efficacité de coût observée.","en":"1. CPI = 108000/140000 = 0.7714.\n2. SPI = 108000/130000 = 0.8308.\n3. EAC = 600000/0.7714 ≈ €777777.7778.\n4. CPI < 1 indicates earned work cost more than its budget; SPI does not establish completion date.\n\nForecast assumes observed cost efficiency continues."}},"exam_08_B_case2_decision":{"answer":{"choice_id":"exam_08_B_case2_decision_c3"},"rubric":{},"explanation":{"fr":"Analyser les livrables acquis, le chemin critique et l’hypothèse de forecast avant de décider. Le forecast suppose la poursuite de l’efficacité de coût observée.","en":"Examine earned deliverables, critical path and forecast assumptions before deciding. Forecast assumes observed cost efficiency continues."}},"exam_08_B_case3_q1":{"answer":{"value":200,"unit":"code","abs_tolerance":0.01},"rubric":{},"explanation":{"fr":"1. Valeur entière = 20/0,1 = 200.\n2. Octets décimaux little-endian : [200, 0] ; hex : [C8, 00].\n3. Lecture inversée : 256×200+0 = 51200 pas ; couple apparent 5120 N·m.\n4. Un aller-retour indépendant vérifie le codage ; domaine, validité et timeout demandent d’autres tests.\n\nLe contrat de cet exercice est uint16. Domaine, saturation et validité demandent des tests supplémentaires.","en":"1. Integer = 20/0.1 = 200.\n2. Little-endian decimal bytes: [200, 0]; hex: [C8, 00].\n3. Reversed decoding: 256×200+0 = 51200 counts; apparent torque 5120 N·m.\n4. An independent round trip checks encoding; range, validity and timeout require additional tests.\n\nThis exercise uses uint16. Range, saturation and validity need additional tests."}},"exam_08_B_case3_q2":{"answer":{"value":5120.0,"unit":"N·m","abs_tolerance":15.36},"rubric":{},"explanation":{"fr":"1. Valeur entière = 20/0,1 = 200.\n2. Octets décimaux little-endian : [200, 0] ; hex : [C8, 00].\n3. Lecture inversée : 256×200+0 = 51200 pas ; couple apparent 5120 N·m.\n4. Un aller-retour indépendant vérifie le codage ; domaine, validité et timeout demandent d’autres tests.\n\nLe contrat de cet exercice est uint16. Domaine, saturation et validité demandent des tests supplémentaires.","en":"1. Integer = 20/0.1 = 200.\n2. Little-endian decimal bytes: [200, 0]; hex: [C8, 00].\n3. Reversed decoding: 256×200+0 = 51200 counts; apparent torque 5120 N·m.\n4. An independent round trip checks encoding; range, validity and timeout require additional tests.\n\nThis exercise uses uint16. Range, saturation and validity need additional tests."}},"exam_08_B_case3_q3":{"answer":{"value":200,"unit":"octet","abs_tolerance":0.01},"rubric":{},"explanation":{"fr":"1. Valeur entière = 20/0,1 = 200.\n2. Octets décimaux little-endian : [200, 0] ; hex : [C8, 00].\n3. Lecture inversée : 256×200+0 = 51200 pas ; couple apparent 5120 N·m.\n4. Un aller-retour indépendant vérifie le codage ; domaine, validité et timeout demandent d’autres tests.\n\nLe contrat de cet exercice est uint16. Domaine, saturation et validité demandent des tests supplémentaires.","en":"1. Integer = 20/0.1 = 200.\n2. Little-endian decimal bytes: [200, 0]; hex: [C8, 00].\n3. Reversed decoding: 256×200+0 = 51200 counts; apparent torque 5120 N·m.\n4. An independent round trip checks encoding; range, validity and timeout require additional tests.\n\nThis exercise uses uint16. Range, saturation and validity need additional tests."}},"exam_08_B_case3_decision":{"answer":{"choice_id":"exam_08_B_case3_decision_c2"},"rubric":{},"explanation":{"fr":"Fixer et tester unité, signe, ordre des octets, domaine et réaction au défaut dans l’ICD. Le contrat de cet exercice est uint16. Domaine, saturation et validité demandent des tests supplémentaires.","en":"Specify and test unit, sign, byte order, range and fault response in the ICD. This exercise uses uint16. Range, saturation and validity need additional tests."}}}'::jsonb) ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
